COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[149,"§Imran\nIn the Holy Quran, Imran has been mentioned in three places:\n1.\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفَىٰ آدَمَ وَنُوحًا وَآلَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَآلَ عِمْرَانَ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ\nAllah did choose Adam and Noah, the family of Abraham, and the family of 'Imran above all people.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-33)\n2.\nإِذْ قَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرَانَ رَبِّ إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِي بَطْنِي مُحَرَّرًا فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّي ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ\nBehold! a woman of 'Imran said: \"O my Lord! I do dedicate unto Thee what is in my womb for Thy special service: So accept this of me: For Thou hearest and knowest all things.\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-35)\n3.\nوَمَرْيَمَ ابْنَتَ عِمْرَانَ الَّتِي أَحْصَنَتْ فَرْجَهَا فَنَفَخْنَا فِيهِ مِن رُّوحِنَا وَصَدَّقَتْ بِكَلِمَاتِ رَبِّهَا وَكُتُبِهِ وَكَانَتْ مِنَ الْقَانِتِينَ\nAnd Mary the daughter of 'Imran, who guarded her chastity; and We breathed into (her body) of Our spirit; and she testified to the truth of the words of her Lord and of His Revelations, and was one of the devout (servants).\n(Quran, Surah-66, At-Tahrim, Verse-12)\nImran, described in the last two verses, was the father of Maryam. But Imran, described in the first verse could either be the father of Maryam(this is the opinion of the majority of scholars) or he could be the father of Musa(as) and Haroon(as) because we come to know from the Bible that the name of the father of Musa(as) and Haroon(as) was also Imran. That is why his family tree is described as under:\nYaqub\nLevi\nKahaat\nImran\n____________________________________\nMaryam Haroon Musa\n(Bible, 6:1-3)\nBut the first opinion seems to be correct because Musa(as) was from the family of Ibrahim(as) and all the prophets of Bani-Israel were from the family of Ibrahim(as) and the last prophet from the tribe of Bani-Israel was Isa(as) whose maternal grandfather was Imran. Allah(swt) chose Isa(as) and his mother from among all the people of the world.\nAnd then from the family of Ismael(as), the son of Ibraheem(as) came the last prophet Muhammad(saws). And Allah(swt) chose both of them specifically for spreading His message."],[150,"§Individual Freedom\nAmong the basic human rights, individual freedom holds great importance. Islam recognizes this individual right and condemns prying into one's personal life and actions:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اجْتَنِبُوا كَثِيرًا مِّنَ الظَّنِّ إِنَّ بَعْضَ الظَّنِّ إِثْمٌ ۖ وَلَا تَجَسَّسُوا وَلَا يَغْتَب بَّعْضُكُم بَعْضًا ۚ أَيُحِبُّ أَحَدُكُمْ أَن يَأْكُلَ لَحْمَ أَخِيهِ مَيْتًا فَكَرِهْتُمُوهُ ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ تَوَّابٌ رَّحِيمٌ\nO you who have believed, avoid much [negative] assumption. Indeed, some assumption is sin. And do not spy or backbite each other. Would one of you like to eat the flesh of his brother when dead? You would detest it. And fear Allah; indeed, Allah is Accepting of repentance and Merciful.\n(Quran, Surah-49, Al-Hujurat, Verse-12)\nIn the above verse, this individual freedom has been specifically highlighted. It has been emphasized in the sahih hadith that even if we come to know of somebody’s faults, we should try to hide them and not spread them. Even if somebody has misused this freedom, speaking about it to others not only goes against the person’s individual freedom but it may cause evil to spread in the society. The Holy Quran says with reference to this:\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ يُحِبُّونَ أَن تَشِيعَ الْفَاحِشَةُ فِي الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ ۚ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ\nIndeed, those who like that immorality should be spread [or publicized] among those who have believed will have a painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter. And Allah knows and you do not know.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-19)\nThat is, publicizing somebody’s faults is equivalent to spreading evil in the society. That is why the Holy Prophet(saws) would simply mention the bad consequences of somebody’s bad actions without taking any names. But this individual freedom is not unlimited. And a person’s individual freedom should not clash with the freedom of others. The individual freedom should also not harm the religion, faith or belief of others. The Holy Quran says in this regard:\nوَلَا تَسُبُّوا الَّذِينَ يَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ فَيَسُبُّوا اللَّهَ عَدْوًا بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ\nAnd do not insult those they invoke other than Allah, lest they insult Allah in enmity without knowledge.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-108)\nThis individual freedom should not mean disobedience to one’s parents. But if parents command their children to do something which is ‘shirk’, then it goes beyond the rights of the parents. The Holy Quran says about this:\n﴿وَوَصَّيْنَا الْإِنسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حَمَلَتْهُ أُمُّهُ وَهْنًا عَلَىٰ وَهْنٍ وَفِصَالُهُ فِي عَامَيْنِ أَنِ اشْكُرْ لِي وَلِوَالِدَيْكَ إِلَيَّ الْمَصِيرُ ١٤ وَإِن جَاهَدَاكَ عَلَىٰ أَن تُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا ۖ وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِي الدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوفًا ۖ وَاتَّبِعْ سَبِيلَ مَنْ أَنَابَ إِلَيَّ ۚ ثُمَّ إِلَيَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَأُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ ١٥﴾\nAnd We have enjoined upon man [care] for his parents. His mother carried him, [increasing her] in weakness upon weakness, and his weaning is in two years. Be grateful to Me and to your parents; to Me is the [final] destination. But if they endeavor to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them but accompany them in [this] world with appropriate kindness and follow the way of those who turn back to Me [in repentance]. Then to Me will be your return, and I will inform you about what you used to do.\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verses-14,15)\nBriefly we can say that the Holy Quran and sahih hadith give many examples of individual freedom and Islam is the first religion where cognizance has been taken of this basic human right and certain rules have been laid down regarding these rights. Adhering to these sound principles of Islam ensures individual freedom while also laying the foundation for an exemplary society. But we should also bear in mind that individual freedom which spreads evil in the society cannot form the basis for an ideal society. So, Islam while granting personal freedom also lays down rules for stopping the spread of evil. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلْتَكُن مِّنكُمْ أُمَّةٌ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى الْخَيْرِ وَيَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ ۚ وَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ\nAnd let there be [arising] from you a nation inviting to [all that is] good, enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong, and those will be the successful.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-104)\nThe qualities of an ideal ruler are as follows:\nالَّذِينَ إِن مَّكَّنَّاهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ أَقَامُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتَوُا الزَّكَاةَ وَأَمَرُوا بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَنَهَوْا عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ ۗ وَلِلَّهِ عَاقِبَةُ الْأُمُورِ\n[And they are] those who, if We give them authority in the land, establish prayer and give zakah and enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong. And to Allah belongs the outcome of [all] matters.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-41)"],[151,"§Injeel\n‘Injeel’ is a Greek word. Its meaning is ‘good news’. Injeel is one of the revelations of Allah(swt).\nنَزَّلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ بِالْحَقِّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَأَنزَلَ التَّوْرَاةَ وَالْإِنجِيلَ\nHe has sent down upon you, [O Muhammad], the Book in truth, confirming what was before it. And He revealed the Torah and the Gospel.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-3)\nThis is corroborated in the Holy Bible. In the book of Mark it says:\nAfter John was put in prison, Jesus went into Galilee, proclaiming the good news of God. “The time has come,” he said. “The kingdom of God has come near. Repent and believe the good news!” (Mark 1:14-15)\nAfter John, his pupil also proclaims the good news. Paul says:\nFor I am not ashamed of the gospel, because it is the power of God that brings salvation to everyone who believes: first to the Jew, then to the Gentile.\n(Bible, Romans, 1:16)\nAt one place, condemning the Christians, Paul says:\nI am astonished that you are so quickly deserting the one who called you to live in the grace of Christ and are turning to a different gospel.\n(Bible, Galatians, 1:6)\nAccording to the Holy Quran, this Injeel was a guidance for mankind:\nوَقَفَّيْنَا عَلَىٰ آثَارِهِم بِعِيسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ التَّوْرَاةِ ۖ وَآتَيْنَاهُ الْإِنجِيلَ فِيهِ هُدًى وَنُورٌ وَمُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ التَّوْرَاةِ وَهُدًى وَمَوْعِظَةً لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ\nAnd We sent, following in their footsteps, Jesus, the son of Mary, confirming that which came before him in the Torah; and We gave him the Gospel, in which was guidance and light and confirming that which preceded it of the Torah as guidance and instruction for the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-46)\nWhere is this Injeel? Nothing can be said about it. It seems that it disappeared after the ascent of Isa(as). Today there exist four Injeels in the Bible. They cannot be the original Injeel which was revealed to Isa(as). We can consider it the story of Isa(as) as described by the author of ‘Qamoos Kitab Mukhaddas’:\n“This Injeel has been written by the pupils of Isa(as) in which the life history of Isa(as) has been described”.\n(See word ‘Injeel’ p:121)\nAt another place he says:\n“In these Injeels, mostly the death and resurrection of Isa(as) have been described”\n(See word ‘Injeel’ p:120)\nIt is therefore clear that it is not the same Injeel which was revealed by Allah(swt) to Isa(as) and which was taught and propagated by Isa(as) and his pupils. Now the question arises as to where the original Injeel is? It is the task of the Christian and Muslim scholars to seek it.\nBut we cannot deny the fact that the four Injeels which form the Bible –Matthew, Mark, Luke and John contain a few preachings of Isa(as). They also contain the prediction about the arrival of the Holy Prophet Muhammad(saws).\nMany Christian scholars also do not consider these Injeels the revelation of God. Not much information exists about who the writer of Injeel was, which the original language was and who translated them. The Holy Quran instructs:\nوَلْيَحْكُمْ أَهْلُ الْإِنجِيلِ بِمَا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ فِيهِ ۚ وَمَن لَّمْ يَحْكُم بِمَا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْفَاسِقُونَ\nAnd let the People of the Gospel judge by what Allah has revealed therein. And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed - then it is those who are the defiantly disobedient.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-47)\nThe people who are addressed here are not the present day Christians but the ones to whom the Injeel was given. But they did not judge justly and instead of monotheism they embraced polytheism and made Isa(as) the son of God (Inna Aoozubillah). If this is what they earnestly believe, they first ought to believe the prediction of Isa(as) that a prophet would arrive after him whose name would be Muhammad(saws)."],[152,"§Insaan\nThe Holy Quran is the last book of revelation of Allah(swt) and it clearly describes the creation of ‘Insaan’ or man. The Vedas, Bible and other religious books do not throw much light on this.\nWhen we gauge the personality of ‘Insaan’ from the verses of the Holy Quran, we can conclude the following:\n1.\nإِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيسَىٰ عِندَ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ آدَمَ ۖ خَلَقَهُ مِن تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ قَالَ لَهُ كُن فَيَكُونُ\nIndeed, the example of Jesus to Allah is like that of Adam. He created Him from dust; then He said to him, \"Be,\" and he was.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-59)\n2.\nالَّذِي أَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقَهُ ۖ وَبَدَأَ خَلْقَ الْإِنسَانِ مِن طِينٍ\nWho perfected everything which He created and began the creation of man from clay.\n(Quran, Surah-32,As-Sajda, Verse-7)\n3.\nإِنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُم مِّن طِينٍ لَّازِبٍ\nIndeed, We created men from sticky clay.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verse-11)\n4.\nخَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِن صَلْصَالٍ كَالْفَخَّارِ\nHe created man from clay like [that of] pottery.\n(Quran, Surah-55, Ar-Rahman, Verse-14)\n5.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ مِن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ\nAnd We did certainly create man out of clay from an altered black mud.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-26)\n6.\nوَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي خَالِقٌ بَشَرًا مِّن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when your Lord said to the angels, \"I will create a human being out of clay from an altered black mud.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-28)\n7.\nقَالَ لَمْ أَكُن لِّأَسْجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهُ مِن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ\nHe said, \"Never would I prostrate to a human whom You created out of clay from an altered black mud.\"\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-33)\nFrom the above verses we understand that Allah(swt) created man from mud which was sticky (clay) and when hardened, it looked like the pottery clay. Then Allah(swt) Himself modelled it.\n﴿إِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي خَالِقٌ بَشَرًا مِّن طِينٍ ٧١ فَإِذَا سَوَّيْتُهُ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيهِ مِن رُّوحِي فَقَعُوا لَهُ سَاجِدِينَ ٧٢﴾\n[So mention] when your Lord said to the angels, \"Indeed, I am going to create a human being from clay. So when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My [created] soul, then fall down to him in prostration.\"\n(Quran, Surah-38, Sad, Verses-71,72)\nAllah(swt) proportioned the clay model in such an excellent way that man became the most superior among His creatures.\nلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ فِي أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ\nWe have certainly created man in the best of stature\n(Quran, Surah-95, At-Tin, Verse-4)\nAnd from it Allah(swt) created its mate (Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-1) and from this pair were born many men and women. It says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿الَّذِي أَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقَهُ ۖ وَبَدَأَ خَلْقَ الْإِنسَانِ مِن طِينٍ ٧ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ نَسْلَهُ مِن سُلَالَةٍ مِّن مَّاءٍ مَّهِينٍ ٨﴾\nWho perfected everything which He created and began the creation of man from clay. Then He made his posterity out of the extract of a liquid disdained.\n(Quran, Surah-32, As-Sajda-7,8)\nAnd this is the same man who behaves so arrogantly on earth.\n1.\nخَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِن نُّطْفَةٍ فَإِذَا هُوَ خَصِيمٌ مُّبِينٌ\nHe created man from a sperm-drop; then at once, he is a clear adversary.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-4)\n2.\nأَوَلَمْ يَرَ الْإِنسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِن نُّطْفَةٍ فَإِذَا هُوَ خَصِيمٌ مُّبِينٌ\nDoes man not consider that We created him from a [mere] sperm-drop - then at once he is a clear adversary?\n(Quran, Surah-36, Yasin, Verse-77)\nThat is, when man is called towards the path of his Creator, he denies the truth and when messengers are sent calling him to the right path, he rejects their message and does not pay any heed to their preachings when in fact the Holy Quran says:\nوَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِي آدَمَ وَحَمَلْنَاهُمْ فِي الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ وَرَزَقْنَاهُم مِّنَ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَفَضَّلْنَاهُمْ عَلَىٰ كَثِيرٍ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقْنَا تَفْضِيلًا\nAnd We have certainly honored the children of Adam and carried them on the land and sea and provided for them of the good things and preferred them over much of what We have created, with [definite] preference.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-70)\nThis superiority has been provided to man so that he may follow the path of Allah(swt) but man is foolishly arrogant and has turned away from the right path. The Holy Quran says:\nوَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن ذُكِّرَ بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِ فَأَعْرَضَ عَنْهَا وَنَسِيَ مَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدَاهُ\nAnd who is more unjust than one who is reminded of the verses of his Lord but turns away from them and forgets what his hands have put forth?\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-57)\nيَا أَيُّهَا الْإِنسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيمِ\nO mankind, what has deceived you concerning your Lord, the Generous.\n(Quran, Surah-82, Al-Infitar, Verse-6)\nAl-Asr is the shortest surah of the Holy Quran. It consists of just three verses. The reality of man is described very subtly in it.\n﴿وَالْعَصْرِ ١ إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لَفِي خُسْرٍ ٢ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالصَّبْرِ ٣﴾\nBy time, Indeed, mankind is in loss, Except for those who have believed and done righteous deeds and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience.\n(Quran, Surah-103, Al-Asr, Verses-1-3)\nIn these verses Allah(swt) has made it clear that the path for ultimate success is unique. Its features are:\nFaith\nGood deeds\nAdvocating the truth\nAdvocating patience\nThat is the reason why Imam Shafai(ra) says that if this surah alone had been revealed, it would be sufficient for the benefit of all human beings.\nOne prominent feature of the Holy Quran is that on one hand it highlights the weaknesses of human beings and on the other hand it says that the ones who overcome these weaknesses and follow the path of Allah(swt) by doing good deeds are the truly successful ones.\nBut this same man turns arrogant and disobedient and does not follow the rules laid down by Allah(swt). He follows the whims and fancies of his heart and creates mischief on earth.\nIn spite of making very clear the difference between good and bad and truth and falsehood, man does not follow the path of Allah(swt) and commits sins against himself and against the whole humanity and spreads mischief on earth. He considers himself above all others and forgets the fact that he is extremely insignificant. Reminding man of his insignificance, the Holy Quran says:\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ مِن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ\nAnd We did certainly create man out of clay from an altered black mud.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-26)\nخَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِن نُّطْفَةٍ فَإِذَا هُوَ خَصِيمٌ مُّبِينٌ\nHe created man from a sperm-drop; then at once, he is a clear adversary.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-4)\nأَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْإِنسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِن قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا\nDoes man not remember that We created him before, while he was nothing?\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verse-67)\n﴿وَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ مِن سُلَالَةٍ مِّن طِينٍ ١٢ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَاهُ نُطْفَةً فِي قَرَارٍ مَّكِينٍ ١٣ ثُمَّ خَلَقْنَا النُّطْفَةَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْعَلَقَةَ مُضْغَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْمُضْغَةَ عِظَامًا فَكَسَوْنَا الْعِظَامَ لَحْمًا ثُمَّ أَنشَأْنَاهُ خَلْقًا آخَرَ ۚ فَتَبَارَكَ اللَّهُ أَحْسَنُ الْخَالِقِينَ ١٤﴾\nAnd certainly did We create man from an extract of clay. Then We placed him as a sperm-drop in a firm lodging. Then We made the sperm-drop into a clinging clot, and We made the clot into a lump [of flesh], and We made [from] the lump, bones, and We covered the bones with flesh; then We developed him into another creation. So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Mu’minun, Verses-12-14)\n﴿الَّذِي أَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقَهُ ۖ وَبَدَأَ خَلْقَ الْإِنسَانِ مِن طِينٍ ٧ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ نَسْلَهُ مِن سُلَالَةٍ مِّن مَّاءٍ مَّهِينٍ ٨ ثُمَّ سَوَّاهُ وَنَفَخَ فِيهِ مِن رُّوحِهِ ۖ وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْأَبْصَارَ وَالْأَفْئِدَةَ ۚ قَلِيلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُونَ ٩﴾\nWho perfected everything which He created and began the creation of man from clay. Then He made his posterity out of the extract of a liquid disdained. Then He proportioned him and breathed into him from His [created] soul and made for you hearing and vision and hearts; little are you grateful.\n(Quran, Surah-32, As-Sajda, Verses-7-9)\n﴿أَوَلَمْ يَرَ الْإِنسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِن نُّطْفَةٍ فَإِذَا هُوَ خَصِيمٌ مُّبِينٌ ٧٧ وَضَرَبَ لَنَا مَثَلًا وَنَسِيَ خَلْقَهُ ۖ قَالَ مَن يُحْيِي الْعِظَامَ وَهِيَ رَمِيمٌ ٧٨ قُلْ يُحْيِيهَا الَّذِي أَنشَأَهَا أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ۖ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ خَلْقٍ عَلِيمٌ ٧٩﴾\nDoes man not consider that We created him from a [mere] sperm-drop - then at once he is a clear adversary? And he presents for Us an example and forgets his [own] creation. He says, \"Who will give life to bones while they are disintegrated?\" Say, \"He will give them life who produced them the first time; and He is, of all creation, Knowing.\"\n(Quran, Surah-36, Ya-Sin, Verses-77-79)\nTo explain the creation of man and the rules of his existence, Allah(swt) has revealed one whole surah ‘Insaan’ which has thirty-one verses. It is also called surah ‘Dahar’. Given below is the translation of a few of its verses:\n﴿هَلْ أَتَىٰ عَلَى الْإِنسَانِ حِينٌ مِّنَ الدَّهْرِ لَمْ يَكُن شَيْئًا مَّذْكُورًا ١ إِنَّا خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ مِن نُّطْفَةٍ أَمْشَاجٍ نَّبْتَلِيهِ فَجَعَلْنَاهُ سَمِيعًا بَصِيرًا ٢ إِنَّا هَدَيْنَاهُ السَّبِيلَ إِمَّا شَاكِرًا وَإِمَّا كَفُورًا ٣﴾\nHas there [not] come upon man a period of time when he was not a thing [even] mentioned? Indeed, We created man from a sperm-drop mixture that We may try him; and We made him hearing and seeing. Indeed, We guided him to the way, be he grateful or be he ungrateful.\n(Quran, Surah-76, Dahar, Verses-1-3)\n﴿إِنَّ هَٰؤُلَاءِ يُحِبُّونَ الْعَاجِلَةَ وَيَذَرُونَ وَرَاءَهُمْ يَوْمًا ثَقِيلًا ٢٧ نَّحْنُ خَلَقْنَاهُمْ وَشَدَدْنَا أَسْرَهُمْ ۖ وَإِذَا شِئْنَا بَدَّلْنَا أَمْثَالَهُمْ تَبْدِيلًا ٢٨ إِنَّ هَٰذِهِ تَذْكِرَةٌ ۖ فَمَن شَاءَ اتَّخَذَ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِ سَبِيلًا ٢٩﴾\nIndeed, these [disbelievers] love the immediate and leave behind them a grave Day. We have created them and strengthened their forms, and when We will, We can change their likenesses with [complete] alteration. Indeed, this is a reminder, so he who wills may take to his Lord a way.\n(Quran, Surah-76, Dahar, Verses-27-29)\nThe bounties of Allah(swt) are innumerable. He created man from nothing but clay, then he created various things for his pleasant stay on this earth, poured rain from the skies, brought forth crops from the earth, created the sun and the moon, the wind and so on. In return Allah(swt) just wanted man to be obedient and worship no one other than Him(swt). He wanted him to follow the rules laid down by Him(swt) and abstain from spreading mischief on this earth. But sadly man has forgotten all this and become an oppressor on this earth. In this regard the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ دَائِبَيْنِ ۖ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ اللَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ ٣٣ وَآتَاكُم مِّن كُلِّ مَا سَأَلْتُمُوهُ ۚ وَإِن تَعُدُّوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ لَا تُحْصُوهَا ۗ إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لَظَلُومٌ كَفَّارٌ ٣٤﴾\nAnd He subjected for you the sun and the moon, continuous [in orbit], and subjected for you the night and the day. And He gave you from all you asked of Him. And if you should count the favor of Allah, you could not enumerate them. Indeed, mankind is [generally] most unjust and ungrateful.\n(Quran, Surah-14, Ibrahim, Verses-33,34)\nوَإِذَا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فِي الْبَحْرِ ضَلَّ مَن تَدْعُونَ إِلَّا إِيَّاهُ ۖ فَلَمَّا نَجَّاكُمْ إِلَى الْبَرِّ أَعْرَضْتُمْ ۚ وَكَانَ الْإِنسَانُ كَفُورًا\nAnd when adversity touches you at sea, lost are [all] those you invoke except for Him. But when He delivers you to the land, you turn away [from Him]. And ever is man ungrateful.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-67)\nوَإِذَا أَنْعَمْنَا عَلَى الْإِنسَانِ أَعْرَضَ وَنَأَىٰ بِجَانِبِهِ ۖ وَإِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ كَانَ يَئُوسًا\nAnd when We bestow favor upon the disbeliever, he turns away and distances himself; and when evil touches him, he is ever despairing.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-83)\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا فِي هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنِ لِلنَّاسِ مِن كُلِّ مَثَلٍ ۚ وَكَانَ الْإِنسَانُ أَكْثَرَ شَيْءٍ جَدَلًا\nAnd We have certainly diversified in this Qur'an for the people from every [kind of] example; but man has ever been, most of anything, [prone to] dispute.\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-54)\n﴿وَيَقُولُ الْإِنسَانُ أَإِذَا مَا مِتُّ لَسَوْفَ أُخْرَجُ حَيًّا ٦٦ أَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْإِنسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِن قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا ٦٧ فَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَحْشُرَنَّهُمْ وَالشَّيَاطِينَ ثُمَّ لَنُحْضِرَنَّهُمْ حَوْلَ جَهَنَّمَ جِثِيًّا ٦٨﴾\nAnd the disbeliever says, \"When I have died, am I going to be brought forth alive?\" Does man not remember that We created him before, while he was nothing? So by your Lord, We will surely gather them and the devils; then We will bring them to be present around Hell upon their knees.\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-66-68)\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْإِنسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيمِ ٦ الَّذِي خَلَقَكَ فَسَوَّاكَ فَعَدَلَكَ ٧ فِي أَيِّ صُورَةٍ مَّا شَاءَ رَكَّبَكَ ٨ كَلَّا بَلْ تُكَذِّبُونَ بِالدِّينِ ٩ وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ لَحَافِظِينَ ١٠ كِرَامًا كَاتِبِينَ ١١ يَعْلَمُونَ مَا تَفْعَلُونَ ١٢ إِنَّ الْأَبْرَارَ لَفِي نَعِيمٍ ١٣ وَإِنَّ الْفُجَّارَ لَفِي جَحِيمٍ ١٤ يَصْلَوْنَهَا يَوْمَ الدِّينِ ١٥ وَمَا هُمْ عَنْهَا بِغَائِبِينَ ١٦ وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّينِ ١٧ ثُمَّ مَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّينِ ١٨ يَوْمَ لَا تَمْلِكُ نَفْسٌ لِّنَفْسٍ شَيْئًا ۖ وَالْأَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ ١٩﴾\nO mankind, what has deceived you concerning your Lord, the Generous, Who created you, proportioned you, and balanced you? In whatever form He willed has He assembled you. No! But you deny the Recompense. And indeed, [appointed] over you are keepers, Noble and recording; They know whatever you do. Indeed, the righteous will be in pleasure, And indeed, the wicked will be in Hellfire. They will [enter to] burn therein on the Day of Recompense, And never therefrom will they be absent. And what can make you know what is the Day of Recompense? Then, what can make you know what is the Day of Recompense? It is the Day when a soul will not possess for another soul [power to do] a thing; and the command, that Day, is [entirely] with Allah.\n(Quran, Surah-82, Al-Infitar, Verses-6-19)\nThat is, on that day no deity, human, angel, prophet or wali will have the power to help anybody in any way. Actually everybody will be busy with his own self. Nobody will help anybody else carry his or her burden. This has been explained in surah An-Najm as follows:\n﴿أَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ ٣٨ وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَانِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ٣٩﴾\nThat no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another. And that there is not for man except that [good] for which he strives.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verses-38,39)\nThen the Holy Quran describes the person who has been successful:\n﴿وَالْعَصْرِ ١ إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لَفِي خُسْرٍ ٢ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالصَّبْرِ ٣﴾\nBy time. Indeed, mankind is in loss. Except for those who have believed and done righteous deeds and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience.\n(Quran, Surah-103, Al-Asr, Verses-1-3)\nThat is, when we set out to explain the truth, numerous difficulties present themselves. But the truly successful person is the one who remains steadfast on the true path and calls others also towards the right path. He bears all the difficulties with patience and advises others also to do the same."],[153,"§Insha-Allah\nThe Muslims have been commanded that when they want to do something in the future, be it the near future or at some later date, they should say ‘Insha-Allah’ which means ‘If Allah(swt) Wills’ or ‘If Allah(swt) Wishes’. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَا تَقُولَنَّ لِشَيْءٍ إِنِّي فَاعِلٌ ذَٰلِكَ غَدًا ٢٣ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ اللَّهُ ۚ﴾\nNor say of anything, \"I shall be sure to do so and so tomorrow\"-\nWithout adding, \"So please Allah!\".\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verses-23-24)\nTomorrow means in the future, be it very soon or sometime later on. In case somebody forgets to say ‘Insha-Allah’, whenever he remembers he should say it:\nوَاذْكُر رَّبَّكَ إِذَا نَسِيتَ وَقُلْ عَسَىٰ أَن يَهْدِيَنِ رَبِّي لِأَقْرَبَ مِنْ هَٰذَا رَشَدًا\nAnd call thy Lord to mind when thou forgettest, and say, \"I hope that my Lord will guide me ever closer (even) than this to the right road.\"\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-24)\nAllah(swt) is All-Powerful while man is totally powerless. So, whatever man wishes to do is impossible till Allah(swt) wishes it. So, it has been ordered that when we refer to some work which we intend to do in future, we should always say ‘Insha-Allah’."],[154,"§Intention (Niyyat)\n‘Niyyat’ or intention is a prominent word in the Islamic terminology which cannot be found in any other religion. This is a very important part of worship and so a brief description is given below:\nBefore any act of worship, when a person decides in his heart that this pious act is solely for the pleasure of Allah(swt), then it is called ‘niyyat’ or intention. And if somebody does not make this intention before an act of worship, then it will not be accepted by Allah(swt).\nAccording to a sahih hadith:\n\"The reward of deeds depends upon the intentions and every person will get the reward according to what he has intended.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1 and Muslim, 1907)\nThat is, if someone does a pious deed for Allah(swt), Allah(swt) shall reward him and if someone does something for someone else, then Allah(swt) will not reward him and will tell him,” Go and ask the person whom you were worshipping for reward,”\nHence, it is extremely important and in fact obligatory to make the intention before any act of worship or pious deed that it is for Allah(swt) alone. It is not necessary to make an oral declaration of ‘niyyat’ but deciding it in our minds will suffice. Only in the case of Hajj is it necessary to verbally make the ‘niyyat’ as follows:\n“Allahumma Labbayak bil Hajj” which means “O Allah(swt)! I am making this intention for Hajj in order to reach You(swt).” All acts of worship and pious deeds should be done solely for the pleasure of Allah(swt) and not for others to see. In fact, in the case of good deeds (Tahajjud salah, optional fasts, helping the needy) other than the obligatory acts (salah, fasting, zakat, Hajj), if the acts are performed secretly, they incur more rewards. According to a sahih hadith:\n“Charity should be done so secretly that the left hand should not get to know how much the right hand has given.”\nActually, making a show of one's deeds is a disease of the heart and the one who is afflicted with this disease does not do good deeds till he is sure that he will be praised for them. Performing good deeds is an excellent virtue and we should do them whether or not somebody is watching because Allah(swt) is surely watching us and His(swt) pleasure should be our ultimate goal. The Holy Quran says:\nوَمَا أُمِرُوا إِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مُخْلِصِينَ لَهُ الدِّينَ حُنَفَاءَ وَيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَيُؤْتُوا الزَّكَاةَ ۚ وَذَٰلِكَ دِينُ الْقَيِّمَةِ\nAnd they were not commanded except to worship Allah, [being] sincere to Him in religion, inclining to truth, and to establish prayer and to give zakah. And that is the correct religion.\n(Quran, Surah-98, Al-Bayyina, Verse-5)\nThat is, do not include anyone else in the worship of Allah(swt)."],[155,"§Intercession (Shafa’at)\nIntercession means intervening or mediating on behalf of somebody. The idol-worshippers of Makka believed that their mud and stone deities would intercede on their behalf with Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\nوَيَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلَا يَنفَعُهُمْ وَيَقُولُونَ هَٰؤُلَاءِ شُفَعَاؤُنَا عِندَ اللَّهِ ۚ قُلْ أَتُنَبِّئُونَ اللَّهَ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَلَا فِي الْأَرْضِ ۚ سُبْحَانَهُ وَتَعَالَىٰ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ\nAnd they worship other than Allah that which neither harms them nor benefits them, and they say, \"These are our intercessors with Allah.\" Say, \"Do you inform Allah of something He does not know in the heavens or on the earth?\" Exalted is He and high above what they associate with Him.\n(Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-18)\nThe Holy Quran describes the following principles for intercession:\n1. If somebody can intercede it is only those who have been given the authority by Allah(swt). That is, somebody can intercede only by the wish of Allah(swt).\n2. Secondly intercession will be only for those with whom Allah(swt) is pleased; that is the people who have believed in and practiced monotheism. Nobody will intercede for the people who have rejected Allah(swt) or ascribed partners to Him(swt) because they will have incurred the wrath of Allah(swt).\nThe Holy Quran says:\nوَكَم مِّن مَّلَكٍ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ لَا تُغْنِي شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا إِلَّا مِن بَعْدِ أَن يَأْذَنَ اللَّهُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ وَيَرْضَىٰ\nAnd how many angels there are in the heavens whose intercession will not avail at all except [only] after Allah has permitted [it] to whom He wills and approves.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-26)\nWho are these who will have the authority to intercede? They are the ones whose intercession will be liked by Allah(swt):\nيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا تَنفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ إِلَّا مَنْ أَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمَٰنُ وَرَضِيَ لَهُ قَوْلًا\nThat Day, no intercession will benefit except [that of] one to whom the Most Merciful has given permission and has accepted his word.\n(Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-109)\nAmong the intercessions, the most important will be the intercession of the Holy Prophet(saws) who will intercede for his(saws) ummat in the grounds of Arafat.\nWhen the sun comes close to the earth and the people will be running here and there panic-stricken, they will wish for somebody who can intercede on their behalf and save them from their present difficulties. They will approach all the prophets like Adam, Nuh, Ibraheem, Musa, Isa(as) but everyone will turn them away saying that their Lord(swt) is furious that day and that they do not have the courage to approach Him(swt) because they had committed such and such a sin in their worldly lives. Then they will approach the Holy Prophet(saws) and he(saws) will fall down in prostration. It will be said to him(saws), “O Muhammad raise your head. Ask what you want to ask?” The Holy Prophet(saws) will say, “My Ummah, my Ummah.” It will be ordered, “Let your ummah into paradise. No account will be taken of their deeds.” (Sahih Bukhari, 4712 and Sahih Muslim, 194)\nThe angels and the other prophets will also intercede on behalf of the believers (momin) (See Bukhari, 7439 and Muslim, 183)\nAmong the interceders will be the martyrs who shall intercede on behalf of seventy of their family members. (See Abu Dawood, 2522)\nThese are the people with whom Allah(swt) is pleased and hence they shall intercede on behalf of only those people who have not committed any form of shirk because Allah(swt) has declared in the case of polytheists (mushrik):\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَن يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَمَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرَىٰ إِثْمًا عَظِيمًا\nIndeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with Allah has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-48)\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَن يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَمَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلَالًا بَعِيدًا\nIndeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with Allah has certainly gone far astray.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-116)\nSo, it is useless even if somebody intercedes on behalf of the polytheists."],[156,"§Interest\nInterest is a social evil which spreads like cancer. The society which is afflicted with this disease becomes weak and unstable. That is why a few ancient tribes used this for their enemies while it was forbidden for them. The Bible has also forbidden interest for its people:\nIf you lend money to one of my people among you who is needy, do not treat it like a business deal; charge no interest. (Bible, Exodus, 22:25)\nWho lends money to the poor without interest; who does not accept a bribe against the innocent. Whoever does these things will never be shaken.\n(Bible, Psalms, 15:5)\n‘Nehemiah’ was furious with the Jews who were charging interest from their brothers. (Nehemiah, 5:6-12)\nThe Bible while forbidding the charging of interest from Jews, allowed it to be charged from the non-Jews:\nDo not charge a fellow Israelite interest, whether on money or food or anything else that may earn interest. You may charge a foreigner interest, but not a fellow Israelite, so that the Lord your God may bless you in everything you put your hand to in the land you are entering to possess.\n(Deuteronomy, 23:19-20)\nThe truth is that even the Jews were forbidden from taking interest. But they persisted in taking interest. First they started taking interest from the non-Jews and then slowly started taking it from the Jews also. That is why Allah(swt) forbade them many things (haram) which were allowed previously (halal).\n(See: Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verses-160-161)\nIn Islam interest has been forbidden, whether it is charged from Muslims or non-Muslims. This is because Islam strives to establish a society in which there is a feeling of compassion and helpfulness between each other and the giving and taking of interest only creates a feeling of hatred and enmity. The people charging interest take advantage of the difficulties of the people who borrow money from them and make their plight a means of their livelihood. In fact, by just loaning money once, the rich enslave the poor because this system of interest and compound interest is such that once the needy person is trapped in it, it is almost impossible to get out of its vicious grasp. So it is impossible to have feelings of good-will and kindness in a society caught in the mire of interest. Hence, the Holy Quran categorically forbids the charging of interest:\nالَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ الرِّبَا لَا يَقُومُونَ إِلَّا كَمَا يَقُومُ الَّذِي يَتَخَبَّطُهُ الشَّيْطَانُ مِنَ الْمَسِّ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَالُوا إِنَّمَا الْبَيْعُ مِثْلُ الرِّبَا ۗ وَأَحَلَّ اللَّهُ الْبَيْعَ وَحَرَّمَ الرِّبَا\nThose who consume interest cannot stand [on the Day of Resurrection] except as one stands who is being beaten by Satan into insanity. That is because they say, \"Trade is [just] like interest.\" But Allah has permitted trade and has forbidden interest.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-275)\nThat is on the Day of Resurrection the people who consume interest will be raised up as demented people. In fact, even in this worldly life they are demented because they are forever thinking up ways and means to suck up the blood of the poor. That is why the Holy Quran clearly commands the believers:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَذَرُوا مَا بَقِيَ مِنَ الرِّبَا إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ٢٧٨ فَإِن لَّمْ تَفْعَلُوا فَأْذَنُوا بِحَرْبٍ مِّنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ۖ وَإِن تُبْتُمْ فَلَكُمْ رُءُوسُ أَمْوَالِكُمْ لَا تَظْلِمُونَ وَلَا تُظْلَمُونَ ٢٧٩﴾\nO you who have believed, fear Allah and give up what remains [due to you] of interest, if you should be believers. And if you do not, then be informed of a war [against you] from Allah and His Messenger. But if you repent, you may have your principal - [thus] you do no wrong, nor are you wronged.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verses-278, 279)\nThat is, the person who has loaned the money may take back the principal but he should repent and not charge interest on it. In that case neither the lender nor the borrower will be wronged. But if he persists in taking interest, then he wages a war against Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws) and the one who does so will be neither successful in this world nor in the Hereafter. He will lead a demented life on this earth like the one whom the Satan has touched. And it is possible that his wealth will be destroyed in an instant. It has been observed that the people taking interest generally lose their wealth in some misfortune. This punishment is in addition to what they shall have to face in the Hereafter.\nInterest can be recompensed with charity as the Holy Quran says:\nيَمْحَقُ اللَّهُ الرِّبَا وَيُرْبِي الصَّدَقَاتِ\nAllah destroys interest and gives increase for charities.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-276)\nAccording to the Holy Quran, interest is an evil in all respects. No good can ensue from it as the Western economists are slowly realizing. Many of them are being attracted to the principles of Islamic economy.\nوَمَا آتَيْتُم مِّن رِّبًا لِّيَرْبُوَ فِي أَمْوَالِ النَّاسِ فَلَا يَرْبُو عِندَ اللَّهِ ۖ وَمَا آتَيْتُم مِّن زَكَاةٍ تُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَ اللَّهِ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُضْعِفُونَ\nAnd whatever you give for interest to increase within the wealth of people will not increase with Allah. But what you give in zakah, desiring the countenance of Allah - those are the multipliers.\n(Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Rum, Verse-39)\nThis means that when interest is added to the existing wealth, it does not in any way benefit the receiver but will be a source of misery for him. On the other hand, zakat does not decrease but increase the wealth and will result in immense benefits from Allah(swt). These are the rewards as far as this earthly life is concerned and the rewards of the Hereafter are beyond our wildest dreams.\nInterest is of two kinds:\n1. First is ‘Riba Al-Nasiah’ or ‘Riba Al-Qarud’ which is a revolving interest on loans. In this case the borrowed amount is returned before the contracted date along with the agreed upon interest. Most of the loans today fall into this category of ‘Riba Al-Nasiah’ because time is crucial in this case. That is, the more the time taken to repay the loan, the more will the interest amount. Sometimes interest accumulates on interest also. Condemning this the Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَأْكُلُوا الرِّبَا أَضْعَافًا مُّضَاعَفَةً ۖ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ\nO you who have believed, do not consume usury, doubled and multiplied, but fear Allah that you may be successful.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-130)\nIn the case of these loans, it generally happens that when the borrower is unable to repay the loan by the contracted date, the lender gives him some more time but at a higher rate of interest. The more the time taken to repay the loan, the more the accumulating interest till a time comes when the interest is much much more than the actual loan and it becomes impossible for the borrower to repay it. He loses all his wealth and property and becomes a pauper. He will have neither a house to stay in, nor food to eat nor proper clothes to wear because the lender will lay claim to all these. The term ‘Aza’afam Muza’afa’ has been used for this in the Holy Quran which means ‘doubled and multiplied’ because in ‘Riba Al-Nasiah’ time is of prime importance and the final amount is many times the original amount. These greedy lenders are being warned in the next verse of the Holy Quran as:\nوَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكَافِرِينَ\nAnd fear the Fire, which has been prepared for the disbelievers.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-131)\nThe believers are being admonished that if they do not desist, then this sin of usury will finally lead them to disbelief because taking interest is equivalent to waging war against Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws). That is why if the restrictions of time and interest are removed from the amount to be returned, only the amount borrowed remains. If the borrower while returning the money gives a little extra as a sign of gratitude, then it will not be considered as interest and in fact such an action is worthy of praise.\n2. The second type is ‘Riba Al-Fazal’. This means to give an increased amount in the barter trade with the same kind of commodities.’Fazal’ means more. According to a sahih hadith:\n“Gold in return for gold, silver in return for silver, wheat in return for wheat, barley in return for barley, dates in return for dates and salt in return for salt, can be traded if and only if they are in the same quantity and that it should be hand to hand. If someone gives more or takes more he has engaged in Riba and accordingly has committed a sin”.\n(Sahih Muslim, 1587)\nThere are many other hadith from which we understand the following:\n1. These commodities which can be traded are of three kinds:\nFirst: Gold and Silver\nSecond: Food items\nThird: Spices or seasonings\nThe above three things are those which fulfill the human needs. To prevent usury in the trading of the above things, Islam has imposed a few restrictions. One is that they should be traded in equal quantities. That is, a kilogram of gold or silver should be traded with one kilogram of gold or silver only. In the same way a kilogram of food grains or salt should be traded against one kilogram of food grains or salt only. The quality of the commodities does not matter. This is to prevent a poor man from falling into the trap of usury.\nThe second restriction is that the trading should be hand in hand. That is, there should be no borrowing. So, if for example someone wishes to trade a kilogram of gold for a kilogram of gold but on loan, then it would not be right and would be called interest. As mentioned previously, time is crucial in case of interest. So, it is essential that the commodities be equal in quantity and also the trading should be hand to hand.\n2. If the trading is between different commodities, then it can be done in any way but the selling should be hand in hand. For example if gold is being traded against silver or wheat against barley, then it is not necessary that the quantities be equal. But the selling should be hand to hand.\n3. But if these things are being traded against some other things, then there are no restrictions. They can be traded in any way. It is not even necessary for them to be hand to hand. For example selling a hundred kilograms of wheat for a gram of gold. Similarly a hundred kilograms of dates for five hundred kilogram food grains. In these cases it is not necessary for the quantities to be equal, but they can be sold in whichever way both the concerned parties agree. If a person wishes to sell a higher quality of rice for a lower quality variety so that he gets more quantity, then he should first sell the higher quality rice and get its price. Then with the money obtained he should buy the lower quality rice. Then there are no restrictions upon him. This is the system of finance in Islam by which it safeguards the rights of the poor and protects him from permanent loss and penury.\nIn modern times all transactions are money-based and hence if someone takes or gives one thousand and one hundred rupees instead of one thousand rupees, then it will be considered interest, whether it is hand on hand or in the form of loan and whether it is through a bank or through an individual. That is why the Islamic scholars have come up with the idea of ‘Islamic banks’ which is based on the principles of shariah; for example ‘Muzarabat’ and ‘Salam’. In the muzarabat deal, a few people put up the capital and a few others do business with it. All the parties involved share the profits and losses according to a few principles.\n‘Salam’ is used in trade wherein the loan taken from a bank is returned based on the principles of ‘salam’. The handbook of Islamic banking can be referred to for more information."],[157,"§Intoxicants\nThe consumption, production and selling of intoxicants are forbidden in Islam:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْأَنصَابُ وَالْأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٩٠ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَاءَ فِي الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَن ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلَاةِ ۖ فَهَلْ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١﴾\nO you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through intoxicants and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-90-91)\nWhen these verses were revealed, Umar(ra) said:\n“O Our Rab! We desist, we desist.” And then the people emptied all the vessels filled with alcohol so that the streams of alcohol started flowing through the streets of Madina. So the Islamic scholars are unanimous in their opinion that the making, selling and drinking of alcohol are all strictly forbidden.\nAnd the Islamic scholars are also unanimous in their opinion that the people who drink alcohol should be whipped forty times. If they do not desist even then they can be whipped eighty times. According to a sahih hadith narrated by Ali(ra), the Holy Prophet(saws) would whip a man who was drunk forty times, Abu Bakr(ra) would also whip him forty times while Umar(ra) would whip him eighty times. All these are sunnah. But I like this (meaning whipping forty times). (Sahih Muslim, 1707).\nThis punishment can only be given by a court of law. For the punishment to be given, the person drinking alcohol should accept his crime or two witnesses should give evidence that they had seen him drinking alcohol. If not, then the sinner gets the benefit of doubt."],[158,"§Invisible or hidden\nActually this whole universe is a mystery and we have very little knowledge about it. But there are five things whose knowledge is with Allah(swt) alone:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ عِندَهُ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ وَيُنَزِّلُ الْغَيْثَ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِي الْأَرْحَامِ ۖ وَمَا تَدْرِي نَفْسٌ مَّاذَا تَكْسِبُ غَدًا ۖ وَمَا تَدْرِي نَفْسٌ بِأَيِّ أَرْضٍ تَمُوتُ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ خَبِيرٌ\nIndeed, Allah [alone] has knowledge of the Hour and sends down the rain and knows what is in the wombs. And no soul perceives what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul perceives in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is Knowing and Acquainted.\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-34)\nIn the Sahih Bukhari five keys of the hidden things have been mentioned, the knowledge of which is with Allah(swt) alone and these are the five things. (See Sahih Bukhari-1039).\nOnly Allah(swt) knows what the womb of a woman contains; that is, what the future of the child growing inside will be. So we should not worry about him and consider him a burden because he shall enter this world and lead his life according to his destiny. That is, he should not be aborted."],[159,"§Irum\nThe tribe of ‘Aad’ is also popular as the tribe of ‘Irum’ who made houses from huge pillars cut out of the rocky mountains. The complete description is given under the head ‘Aad’. At one place in the Holy Quran, it is said regarding Irum:\nإِرَمَ ذَاتِ الْعِمَادِ\nOf the (city of) Iram, with lofty pillars.\n(Quran, Surah-89, Al-Fajr, Verse-7)\nWhat is Irum? Some scholars are of the opinion that a person in that was named Irum and eventually the whole tribe was called by that name. A few scholars are of the opinion that reference is made to those people who built their homes out of huge rocks in mountains which is called ‘Rasham’ in Hebrew which means ‘signs’.The tribe referred here is the ‘Aad’ tribe who built houses in the mountains, known today as Madayan Saleh. Even today inscriptions are found on their houses in Aarami and Samud languages."],[160,"§Isa(as)\nIsa(as) is among the prominent prophets of Allah(swt). He was the last prophet from the tribe of Bani-Israel. History says that in the approximately 570 years between Isa(as) and Prophet Muhammad(saws), no prophet was sent to earth.\nThe life of Isa(as) can be divided into three parts:\n1. His birth\n2. Good news about his prophethood\n3. His departure from this world\nThe birth of Isa(as) was a miracle because he was born when Allah(swt) uttered the single word ‘Kun’ which means ‘Be’ and he himself declared that he was the slave of Allah(swt) and that nobody else is worthy of worship except Him(swt). The Holy Quran explains this in great detail:\nإِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنْهُ اسْمُهُ الْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ وَجِيهًا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ\nBehold! the angels said: \"O Mary! Allah giveth thee glad tidings of a Word from Him: his name will be Christ Jesus, the son of Mary, held in honour in this world and the Hereafter and of (the company of) those nearest to Allah;\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-45)\nThis Word is the word ‘Kun’ (Be!) of Allah(swt) upon uttering which anything is possible. He does not need any means for fulfilling His command.\nWhen Jibrail(as) came with the glad tidings to Maryam, she was scared:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ مَرْيَمَ إِذِ انتَبَذَتْ مِنْ أَهْلِهَا مَكَانًا شَرْقِيًّا ١٦ فَاتَّخَذَتْ مِن دُونِهِمْ حِجَابًا فَأَرْسَلْنَا إِلَيْهَا رُوحَنَا فَتَمَثَّلَ لَهَا بَشَرًا سَوِيًّا ١٧ قَالَتْ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِالرَّحْمَٰنِ مِنكَ إِن كُنتَ تَقِيًّا ١٨ قَالَ إِنَّمَا أَنَا رَسُولُ رَبِّكِ لِأَهَبَ لَكِ غُلَامًا زَكِيًّا ١٩ قَالَتْ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَامٌ وَلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِي بَشَرٌ وَلَمْ أَكُ بَغِيًّا ٢٠ قَالَ كَذَٰلِكِ قَالَ رَبُّكِ هُوَ عَلَيَّ هَيِّنٌ ۖ وَلِنَجْعَلَهُ آيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِّنَّا ۚ وَكَانَ أَمْرًا مَّقْضِيًّا ٢١﴾\nRelate in the Book (the story of) Mary, when she withdrew from her family to a place in the East. She placed a screen (to screen herself) from them; then We sent her our angel, and he appeared before her as a man in all respects. She said: \"I seek refuge from thee to (Allah) Most Gracious: (come not near) if thou dost fear Allah.\" He said: \"Nay, I am only a messenger from thy Lord, (to announce) to thee the gift of a holy son. She said: \"How shall I have a son, seeing that no man has touched me, and I am not unchaste?\" He said: \"So (it will be): Thy Lord saith, 'that is easy for Me: and (We wish) to appoint him as a Sign unto men and a Mercy from Us':It is a matter (so) decreed.\"\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-16-21)\nPublic slander against Maryam and the child’s reply to it:\n﴿فَأَتَتْ بِهِ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهُ ۖ قَالُوا يَا مَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا ٢٧ يَا أُخْتَ هَارُونَ مَا كَانَ أَبُوكِ امْرَأَ سَوْءٍ وَمَا كَانَتْ أُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا ٢٨ فَأَشَارَتْ إِلَيْهِ ۖ قَالُوا كَيْفَ نُكَلِّمُ مَن كَانَ فِي الْمَهْدِ صَبِيًّا ٢٩ قَالَ إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ آتَانِيَ الْكِتَابَ وَجَعَلَنِي نَبِيًّا ٣٠ وَجَعَلَنِي مُبَارَكًا أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُ وَأَوْصَانِي بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا ٣١ وَبَرًّا بِوَالِدَتِي وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِي جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا ٣٢ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدتُّ وَيَوْمَ أَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ أُبْعَثُ حَيًّا ٣٣ ذَٰلِكَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ۚ قَوْلَ الْحَقِّ الَّذِي فِيهِ يَمْتَرُونَ ٣٤﴾\nAt length she brought the (babe) to her people, carrying him (in her arms). They said: \"O Mary! truly an amazing thing hast thou brought! \"O sister of Aaron! Thy father was not a man of evil, nor thy mother a woman unchaste!\" But she pointed to the babe. They said: \"How can we talk to one who is a child in the cradle?\" He said: \"I am indeed a servant of Allah: He hath given me revelation and made me a prophet; \"And He hath made me blessed wheresoever I be, and hath enjoined on me Prayer and Charity as long as I live; \"(He) hath made me kind to my mother, and not overbearing or miserable; \"So peace is on me the day I was born, the day that I die, and the day that I shall be raised up to life (again)\"! Such (was) Jesus the son of Mary: (it is) a statement of truth, about which they (vainly) dispute.\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-27-34)\nFor information about the childhood of Isa(as) we have no other source other than the Holy Bible. We come to know from the Bible, that Maryam went away to Egypt along with the baby Isa(as) and her husband-to-be Yusuf because the Roman king Herodes was plotting to kill the child. There is no sound historical proof as to the number of years they stayed there. If it is assumed that Herodes died in 4 B.C. and Isa(as) was born in 5 B.C., then we understand that they were there for a very short time. As to the discrepancy in the B.C years, the Christian scholars themselves concede that there has been an error of 5 years. They returned to Jerusalem after the death of Herodes and started living in the city of Nasira. It is for this reason that they are called ‘Nasiri’ and from this word originated the word ‘Nasara’ which is used in the Holy Quran in many places.\nThen Yusuf passed away and Isa(as) took up carpentry to support himself and his mother. He spent his spare time in studying ‘Tanakh’ which was the religious book of the Jews and is based on the Taurah of Musa(as), the book of the prophets of Bani-Israel and their history. This is known as the Old Testament.\nThere is no information about Isa(as) from when he was 12 years old to when he was 30. He had prophesied about his being a prophet when he was a mere baby, and when he turned thirty he set out on his mission of prophethood, that is spreading the message of Allah(swt). And then he also started performing miracles by the power of Allah(swt):\nوَآتَيْنَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ الْبَيِّنَاتِ وَأَيَّدْنَاهُ بِرُوحِ الْقُدُسِ ۗ\nWe gave Jesus the son of Mary Clear (Signs) and strengthened him with the holy spirit.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-87)\nHis miracles:\nThe Bible says that he performed countless miracles but the Holy Quran describes seven:\n1. His speaking when he was still in the cradle (Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-110).\n2. Making a bird from clay and blowing life into it which with the leave of Allah(swt) became a real bird and started flying. (Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-49).\n3. Curing a person who was born blind (Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-49).\n4. Curing the lepers (Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-49).\n5. Giving life to the dead (Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-49).\n6. Telling the people what they had eaten. (Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-49).\n7. Telling whatever the people have gathered in their houses (Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-49).\nWith these miracles Isa(as) began spreading the message of Allah(swt).\nIt says in the Bible:\n“Isa would visit all the religious places and preached in the synagogues and gave good news and cured people of all kinds of diseases and weaknesses” (Injeel, Matthew, 4:23)\nIsa(as) was sent as a messenger to the tribe of Bani-Israel:\nوَإِذْ قَالَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ إِنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُم مُّصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيَّ مِنَ التَّوْرَاةِ\nAnd remember, Jesus, the son of Mary, said: \"O Children of Israel! I am the messenger of Allah (sent) to you, confirming the Law (which came) before me (Taurah). (Quran, Surah-61, As-Saff, Verse-6)\nوَرَسُولًا إِلَىٰ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ\nAnd (appoint him)(Isa) a messenger to the Children of Israel,\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-49)\nIn the preceding verse it says:\nوَيُعَلِّمُهُ الْكِتَابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَالتَّوْرَاةَ وَالْإِنجِيلَ\n\"And Allah will teach him the Book and Wisdom, the Law and the Gospel,\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-48)\nIsa(as) would preach Taurah only because it contained the instructions to the Bani-Israel for leading a good life. With the help of the book of wisdom namely Injeel, he threw light on the teachings of Taurah. Thus it is clear that Isa(as) was sent as a messenger not for the entire mankind but specifically for the Bani-Israel.\nMatthew in his version of Injeel relates the story of the ‘Canoni Woman’ who came to Isa(as) to free her daughter from an evil spirit. Isa(as) replies:\n“I was not sent for anyone but the sheep of the Israel household who have gone astray”\n(Bible, Matthew, 15:24)\nHe meant that because she was not an Israelite, he could not solve her problem.\nProphecy about Muhammad(saws): The prophecy about the messenger for the entire mankind which is made in the Bible is explained in the Holy Quran as follows:\nوَمُبَشِّرًا بِرَسُولٍ يَأْتِي مِن بَعْدِي اسْمُهُ أَحْمَدُ\nGiving Glad Tidings of a Messenger to come after me, whose name shall be Ahmad.\n(Quran, Surah-61, As-Saff, Verse-6)\nRejecting the prophethood of both the messengers by the Jews: The Jews not only disbelieved the prophet Isa(as) who was sent to them but also rejected the prophethood of Muhammad(saws). The main reason why they rejected both the prophets was because they tried to stop the Jews from committing atrocities. Both of them chastised the Jews for not following the religious books revealed by Allah(swt) and criticized their religious scholars for making changes in the books. And moreover they called the people towards monotheism which was what all the other prophets did:\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ۖ وَقَالَ الْمَسِيحُ يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُ مَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَأْوَاهُ النَّارُ ۖ وَمَا لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنصَارٍ\nThey do blaspheme who say: \"Allah is Christ the son of Mary.\" But said Christ: \"O Children of Israel! worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord.\" Whoever joins other gods with Allah,- Allah will forbid him the garden, and the Fire will be his abode. There will for the wrong-doers be no one to help.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-72)\nThe Jews thought that the messenger would be a king who would save them from the atrocities of others. But when they saw that he was born in a poor family, earned his living through carpentry and criticized them for their shortcomings and wrong actions, they rejected him. And they started tormenting him so much that he started praying for the destruction of Jerusalem. A few examples from the Bible are given below:\nIsa(as) said, “When you see Jerusalem surrounded by armies, then know that its end is near.” (Bible, Luke, 21:20)\n“Jerusalem, Jerusalem, you who kill the prophets and stone those sent to you, how often I have longed to gather your children together, as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings, and you were not willing.” (Bible, Matthew, 23:37)\nA sect of the Jews called ‘Pharisees’ who originated around 135-105 B.C. were the worst enemies of Isa(as). So much so that Isa(as) himself cursed them:\n“Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You shut the door of the kingdom of heaven in people’s faces. You yourselves do not enter, nor will you let those enter who are trying to.\n“Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You travel over land and sea to win a single convert, and when you have succeeded, you make them twice as much a child of hell as you are.\n“Woe to you, blind guides! You say, ‘If anyone swears by the temple, it means nothing; but anyone who swears by the gold of the temple is bound by that oath.’ You blind fools! Which is greater: the gold, or the temple that makes the gold sacred? You also say, ‘If anyone swears by the altar, it means nothing; but anyone who swears by the gift on the altar is bound by that oath.’ You blind men! Which is greater: the gift, or the altar that makes the gift sacred? Therefore, anyone who swears by the altar swears by it and by everything on it. And anyone who swears by the temple swears by it and by the one who dwells in it. And anyone who swears by heaven swears by God’s throne and by the one who sits on it.\n“Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You give a tenth of your spices—mint, dill and cumin. But you have neglected the more important matters of the law—justice, mercy and faithfulness. You should have practiced the latter, without neglecting the former. You blind guides! You strain out a gnat but swallow a camel.\n“Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside they are full of greed and self-indulgence. Blind Pharisee! First clean the inside of the cup and dish, and then the outside also will be clean.\n“Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You are like whitewashed tombs, which look beautiful on the outside but on the inside are full of the bones of the dead and everything unclean.\nIn the same way, on the outside you appear to people as righteous but on the inside you are full of hypocrisy and wickedness.\n“Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You build tombs for the prophets and decorate the graves of the righteous. And you say, ‘If we had lived in the days of our ancestors, we would not have taken part with them in shedding the blood of the prophets.’ So you testify against yourselves that you are the descendants of those who murdered the prophets. Go ahead, then, and complete what your ancestors started!\n“You snakes! You brood of vipers! How will you escape being condemned to hell?\n(Bible, Matthew, 23:13-33)\nFor more information see Matthew, 5:20, 16:6, 11, 12, 23:1-39\nThese same Pharisees succeeded in their evil plot and convinced the Roman Emperor to order the crucifixion of Isa(as).\nDeparture of Isa(as) from this earth: This group of Pharisees convinced the Roman Emperor that not only was Isa(as) preaching against their religion but was also a great danger to their kingdom as well. So, the king ordered Isa(as) to be crucified. The Roman army started searching for Isa(as) but Allah(swt) caused a person ‘Yahuzaiskaryuti’ to look like Isa(as) and the soldiers arrested him because he was the one who gave away the hiding place of Isa(as) to the enemies. He kept shouting, “I am not Isa”, but the soldiers paid no heed and he was crucified.\n(Injeel Barnabas, part 215 and 216)\nThis has been clearly explained in the Holy Quran that they neither killed him nor crucified him:\nوَقَوْلِهِمْ إِنَّا قَتَلْنَا الْمَسِيحَ عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَمَا قَتَلُوهُ وَمَا صَلَبُوهُ وَلَٰكِن شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ ۚ\nThat they said (in boast), \"We killed Christ Jesus the son of Mary, the Messenger of Allah\";- but they killed him not, nor crucified him, but so it was made to appear to them,\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-157)\nWe believe that Isa(as) was taken up alive up into the sky and he will descend again to the earth before the Last Day and break the cross because prostrating before the cross or holding it in high esteem is against his teachings. His main instruction was to pray to Allah(swt) alone:\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ۖ وَقَالَ الْمَسِيحُ يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُ مَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَأْوَاهُ النَّارُ ۖ وَمَا لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنصَارٍ\nThey do blaspheme who say: \"Allah is Christ the son of Mary.\" But said Christ: \"O Children of Israel! worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord.\" Whoever joins other gods with Allah,- Allah will forbid him the garden, and the Fire will be his abode. There will for the wrong-doers be no one to help.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-72)\nIn the same way Isa(as) will kill the pig as is narrated in the Sahih Hadith (Bukhari, 3448 and Muslim, 155) because the pig is an unclean animal and just as it is forbidden to eat it in the Holy Quran, it is declared unlawful in the Taurah.\nLike a gold ring in a pig’s snout is a beautiful woman who shows no discretion.\n(Bible, Proverbs, 11:22)\nHere the woman is compared with the pig because the pig is an unclean and dirty creature. In the book Leviticus, part 11 of the Taurah, the description of the clean and unclean animals is given clearly in lines 7-8.\n“The pig which has a split hoof but does not chew cud and so is unclean for you. Do not eat anything of its flesh and do not even touch its Loth, it is unclean for you.”\nMatthew himself has mentioned in his Injeel that the pig is unclean.\nBut ‘Paulus’ made many changes in the religion of the God propagated by Isa(as). One of them was to make the meat of swine lawful. The majoosi people (fire-worshippers) who were embracing Christianity and were used to eating the flesh of swine were unwilling to stop it; Paulus made it lawful and thus all the other Christians also started eating it. So, Isa(as) will kill the pig and reestablish the original unadulterated religion.’Dajjal’ will also be killed by Isa(as).\nAfter Isa(as) departed from this world and was raised up to heaven, his followers started worshipping him:\nلَّقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ ثَالِثُ ثَلَاثَةٍ ۘ وَمَا مِنْ إِلَٰهٍ إِلَّا إِلَٰهٌ وَاحِدٌ ۚ وَإِن لَّمْ يَنتَهُوا عَمَّا يَقُولُونَ لَيَمَسَّنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ\nThey do blaspheme who say: Allah is one of three in a Trinity: for there is no god except One Allah. If they desist not from their word (of blasphemy), verily a grievous penalty will befall the blasphemers among them.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-73)\nلَّقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ۚ قُلْ فَمَن يَمْلِكُ مِنَ اللَّهِ شَيْئًا إِنْ أَرَادَ أَن يُهْلِكَ الْمَسِيحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَأُمَّهُ وَمَن فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا\nIn blasphemy indeed are those that say that Allah is Christ the son of Mary. Say: \"Who then hath the least power against Allah, if His will were to destroy Christ the son of Mary, his mother, and all every - one that is on the earth?\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-17)\nThe followers of Isa(as) who started worshipping him will be disowned by him on the Day of Judgement. Isa(as) preached monotheism like all the other true prophets and he never asked his followers to either worship him or his mother. This has been explained very beautifully in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ اللَّهُ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ أَأَنتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَٰهَيْنِ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِي أَنْ أَقُولَ مَا لَيْسَ لِي بِحَقٍّ ۚ إِن كُنتُ قُلْتُهُ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهُ ۚ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِي وَلَا أَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِكَ ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ ١١٦ مَا قُلْتُ لَهُمْ إِلَّا مَا أَمَرْتَنِي بِهِ أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمْ ۚ وَكُنتُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيدًا مَّا دُمْتُ فِيهِمْ ۖ فَلَمَّا تَوَفَّيْتَنِي كُنتَ أَنتَ الرَّقِيبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ وَأَنتَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ ١١٧ إِن تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ ۖ وَإِن تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَإِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ ١١٨ قَالَ اللَّهُ هَٰذَا يَوْمُ يَنفَعُ الصَّادِقِينَ صِدْقُهُمْ ۚ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا أَبَدًا ۚ رَّضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوا عَنْهُ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ ١١٩ لِلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَمَا فِيهِنَّ ۚ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ١٢٠﴾\nAnd behold! Allah will say: \"O Jesus the son of Mary! Didst thou say unto men, worship me and my mother as gods in derogation of Allah'?\" He will say: \"Glory to Thee! never could I say what I had no right (to say). Had I said such a thing, thou wouldst indeed have known it. Thou knowest what is in my heart, Thou I know not what is in Thine. For Thou knowest in full all that is hidden. \"Never said I to them aught except what Thou didst command me to say, to wit, 'worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord'; and I was a witness over them whilst I dwelt amongst them; when Thou didst take me up Thou wast the Watcher over them, and Thou art a witness to all things. \"If Thou dost punish them, they are Thy servant: If Thou dost forgive them, Thou art the Exalted in power, the Wise.\" Allah will say: \"This is a day on which the truthful will profit from their truth: theirs are gardens, with rivers flowing beneath,- their eternal Home: Allah well-pleased with them, and they with Allah: That is the great salvation, (the fulfilment of all desires). To Allah doth belong the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and all that is therein, and it is He Who hath power over all things.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-116-120)"],[161,"§Isha\nIsha is the salah offered in the night and the last of the five obligatory salahs. Isha is described as follows in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لِيَسْتَأْذِنكُمُ الَّذِينَ مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ وَالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَبْلُغُوا الْحُلُمَ مِنكُمْ ثَلَاثَ مَرَّاتٍ ۚ مِّن قَبْلِ صَلَاةِ الْفَجْرِ وَحِينَ تَضَعُونَ ثِيَابَكُم مِّنَ الظَّهِيرَةِ وَمِن بَعْدِ صَلَاةِ الْعِشَاءِ ۚ ثَلَاثُ عَوْرَاتٍ لَّكُمْ ۚ لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَا عَلَيْهِمْ جُنَاحٌ بَعْدَهُنَّ ۚ طَوَّافُونَ عَلَيْكُم بَعْضُكُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الْآيَاتِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ\nO ye who believe! let those whom your right hands possess, and the (children) among you who have not come of age ask your permission (before they come to your presence), on three occasions: before morning prayer; the while ye doff your clothes for the noonday heat; and after the late-night prayer: these are your three times of undress: outside those times it is not wrong for you or for them to move about attending to each other: Thus does Allah make clear the Signs to you: for Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-58)\nIt is clear from above that Isha is the last salah in the night after which it is advised to go to sleep.\nThe Isha salah is the last means of communication between Allah(swt) and His slaves so that after toiling the whole day, the slave remembers his Lord(swt), thanks Him for everything and finally goes off to a peaceful sleep with pleasant thoughts of his Allah(swt). We come to know from Sahih Hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) preferred to delay his Isha prayer so that he could go off to sleep immediately after without again getting involved in worldly matters and thus be able to get up fresh for the Tahajjud prayers.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 547, Sahih Muslim, 647)\nBut if any problem arose, he would stay up during the night and try to solve it.\n(Tirmizi, 169)\nThe time for Isha begins when the moon in its third phase starts setting and ends at midnight. But if due to some compelling reason, we cannot offer it before midnight, then it should compulsorily be offered before the time for the Fajr prayer begins. It is narrated in the Sahih Hadith:\nThe time for a particular prayer ends when the time for the next prayer begins.\nSo, the time for the Isha prayer is till the time for the Fajr prayer begins. But many scholars stress that it is best to offer a prayer as soon as the time for it begins.\nThe importance of the Isha prayer: The importance of the Isha prayer is stressed in many Sahih Hadith. One Sahih Hadith says:\nThe hypocrites find the Fajr and the Isha salahs to be very tough. If only they knew the benefits of these prayers, they would come dragging their feet.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 657 and Sahih Muslim, 651)\nSimilarly another Sahih Hadith says:\nOne who has offered the Isha salah in a congregation is like the one who has prayed half the night and the one who has offered both the Isha and Fajr salahs in a congregation is like the one who has prayed the whole night.\n(Sahih Muslim, 656)"],[162,"§Ishaq(as)\nIshaq was the second son of Ibraheem(as). According to the Holy Quran, the glad tidings about his birth was given as follows:\n﴿وَامْرَأَتُهُ قَائِمَةٌ فَضَحِكَتْ فَبَشَّرْنَاهَا بِإِسْحَاقَ وَمِن وَرَاءِ إِسْحَاقَ يَعْقُوبَ ٧١ قَالَتْ يَا وَيْلَتَىٰ أَأَلِدُ وَأَنَا عَجُوزٌ وَهَٰذَا بَعْلِي شَيْخًا ۖ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَشَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ ٧٢ قَالُوا أَتَعْجَبِينَ مِنْ أَمْرِ اللَّهِ ۖ رَحْمَتُ اللَّهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ عَلَيْكُمْ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ ۚ إِنَّهُ حَمِيدٌ مَّجِيدٌ ٧٣﴾\nAnd his Wife was standing, and she smiled. Then We gave her good tidings of Isaac and after Isaac, Jacob. She said, \"Woe to me! Shall I give birth while I am an old woman and this, my husband, is an old man? Indeed, this is an amazing thing!\" They said, \"Are you amazed at the decree of Allah? May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, people of the house. Indeed, He is Praiseworthy and Honorable.\"\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verses-71-73)\nThe first wife of Ibraheem(as), Sara was amazed because she was barren and an old woman of ninety while her husband was already hundred. So, she was surprised when she was given the happy news about the birth of two sons. One other reason was that ladies are generally ashamed to have children at such an advanced age and fear that the other ladies may taunt them. For this reason she started beating herself.\nIshaq(as) was also made a prophet by Allah(swt). It is mentioned in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَبَشَّرْنَاهُ بِإِسْحَاقَ نَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ١١٢﴾\nAnd We gave him good tidings of Isaac, a prophet from among the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verse-112)\nWhen Ishaq(as) was thirty seven years old, his mother Sara passed away. Ibraheem(as) buried her in a cave in Maqfila (See Genesis, 23:19). This is situated in Habroon. It is now known as Al-Khaleel. It is at a distance of 19 miles from Baitul-Muqaddas and 13 miles from Baitul-Laham.\nIshaq(as) was born in the city of Habroon in 2235 B.C. When he turned thirty, Ibraheem(as) got him a wife from his tribe Haraan (Genesis, 24:4). Twenty years later he was blessed with twins. One was named Esau and the other Yaqub (Genesis, 25:21-26) and when he was seventy five, his father Ibraheem(as) passed away. Ishaq buried him near his wife Sara. When there was a drought in the area, he went away to the city of Garaar. There the king Abimelech gave him many camels and sheep and Ishaq(as) prayed for him.\nYaqub, the second son of Ishaq(as) is also called Israel. The people of Bani-Israel were his descendants. He left Garaar along with his children and settled in Beersheba which is about 28 miles to the south of Habroon. There he passed away at the age of 180 and was buried near his parents Ibraheem(as) and Sara.\nIn the Taurah, it has been distorted that the son whom Ibraheem(as) decided to sacrifice was Ishaq(as).\nIn the Taurah itself it is given:\nThen God said, “Take your son, your only son, whom you love—Isaac—and go to the region of Moriah. Sacrifice him there as a burnt offering on a mountain I will show you.” (Genesis, 22:2)\nAnd it is a fact that Ismael was the only son till Ishaq was born. And moreover Ibraheem(as) loved Ismael more than Ishaq because Ismael was his first-born. And the Lord had also promised that he would produce a huge nation through Ismael(Genesis, 21:18). So, Ishaq was not the only son but Ismael was and he was alive even after the death of Ibraheem(as).\nAnd it is even obvious from the Holy Quran that the son who was sacrificed was Ismael(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-101-111) and describing both, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَبَارَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَىٰ إِسْحَاقَ ۚ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهِ مُبِينٌ ١١٣﴾\nAnd We blessed him and Isaac. But among their descendants is the doer of good and the clearly unjust to himself.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verse-113)\nThe tribe of Arabs were the descendants of Ismael(as) and Bani-Israel those of Ishaq(as) which is also the tribe of his sons Yaqub and Mansub. Yaqub had twelve sons and they were:\n1. Reuben 2. Simeon 3. Levi 4. Judah 5. Issachar 6. Zebulun 7. Joseph 8. Benjamin 9. Dan 10. Naphtali 11. Gad 12. Asher\n(See Genesis, 25:13-14)\nThese twelve sons formed the twelve tribes of Bani-Israel and they are described again and again in the Taurah."],[163,"§Islam\nIslam means ‘peace’. Therefore the religion of Islam means ‘the religion which gives peace’. The word ‘silm’ is derived from this. The Holy Quran says:\nوَإِن جَنَحُوا لِلسَّلْمِ فَاجْنَحْ لَهَا وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ\nAnd if they incline to peace, then incline to it [also] and rely upon Allah. Indeed, it is He who is the Hearing, the Knowing.\n(Quran, Surah-8, Al-Anfal, Verse-61)\nThat is, if a war is going on and the enemy sends a message seeking a peace pact, then it should be accepted. In this way, embracing Islam means to submit to the will of Allah(swt):\nفَإِنْ أَسْلَمُوا فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوا ۖ وَّإِن تَوَلَّوْا فَإِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ الْبَلَاغُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِالْعِبَادِ\nAnd if they submit [in Islam], they are rightly guided; but if they turn away - then upon you is only the [duty of] notification. And Allah is Seeing of [His] servants.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-20)\nMoreover, this is not a new religion but it was the religion of all the prophets:\nإِنَّا أَنزَلْنَا التَّوْرَاةَ فِيهَا هُدًى وَنُورٌ ۚ يَحْكُمُ بِهَا النَّبِيُّونَ الَّذِينَ أَسْلَمُوا لِلَّذِينَ هَادُوا وَالرَّبَّانِيُّونَ وَالْأَحْبَارُ بِمَا اسْتُحْفِظُوا مِن كِتَابِ اللَّهِ وَكَانُوا عَلَيْهِ شُهَدَاءَ\nIndeed, We sent down the Torah, in which was guidance and light. The prophets who submitted [to Allah] judged by it for the Jews, as did the rabbis and scholars by that with which they were entrusted of the Scripture of Allah, and they were witnesses thereto.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-44)\nمَا كَانَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ يَهُودِيًّا وَلَا نَصْرَانِيًّا وَلَٰكِن كَانَ حَنِيفًا مُّسْلِمًا وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ\nAbraham was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but he was one inclining toward truth, a Muslim [submitting to Allah]. And he was not of the polytheists.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-67)\nProphet Yusuf(as) prayed to Allah(swt):\nفَاطِرَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ أَنتَ وَلِيِّي فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ ۖ تَوَفَّنِي مُسْلِمًا وَأَلْحِقْنِي بِالصَّالِحِينَ\nCreator of the heavens and earth, You are my protector in this world and in the Hereafter. Cause me to die a Muslim and join me with the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-101)\nوَإِذْ أَوْحَيْتُ إِلَى الْحَوَارِيِّينَ أَنْ آمِنُوا بِي وَبِرَسُولِي قَالُوا آمَنَّا وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّنَا مُسْلِمُونَ\nAnd [remember] when I inspired to the disciples, \"Believe in Me and in My messenger Jesus.\" They said, \"We have believed, so bear witness that indeed we are Muslims [in submission to Allah].\"\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-111)\nقَالَ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ أَيُّكُمْ يَأْتِينِي بِعَرْشِهَا قَبْلَ أَن يَأْتُونِي مُسْلِمِينَ\n[Solomon] said, \"O assembly [of jinn], which of you will bring me her (Queen of Sheba) throne before they come to me in submission?\"\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-38)\nFrom the above verses it becomes clear that the religion propagated by the Holy Prophet(saws) namely Islam was also the religion followed by all the earlier prophets. This is not a new religion:\nقُلْ مَا كُنتُ بِدْعًا مِّنَ الرُّسُلِ وَمَا أَدْرِي مَا يُفْعَلُ بِي وَلَا بِكُمْ ۖ إِنْ أَتَّبِعُ إِلَّا مَا يُوحَىٰ إِلَيَّ وَمَا أَنَا إِلَّا نَذِيرٌ مُّبِينٌ\nSay, \"I am not something original among the messengers, nor do I know what will be done with me or with you. I only follow that which is revealed to me, and I am not but a clear warner.\"\n(Quran, Surah-46, Al-Ahqaf, Verse-9)\nإِنَّ الدِّينَ عِندَ اللَّهِ الْإِسْلَامُ\nIndeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-19)\nوَمَن يَبْتَغِ غَيْرَ الْإِسْلَامِ دِينًا فَلَن يُقْبَلَ مِنْهُ وَهُوَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِينَ\nAnd whoever desires other than Islam as religion - never will it be accepted from him, and he, in the Hereafter, will be among the losers.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-85)\nFrom this we understand that Islam was the religion given to the last Prophet and Messenger Muhammad(saws) and with him came to an end the chain of prophets. No other religion other than Islam will be accepted by Allah(swt) from His slaves. He has made Islam very easy. There is no real difficulty in it. He has not made it a burden for His slaves which they do not have the strength to carry. Islam is based on monotheism. Its distinguishing features are truth, justice and kindness towards each other. It is the only religion which encourages all profitable and good deeds while forbidding the loss-incurring and bad deeds. It is the religion in which Allah(swt) makes pure the faith and actions of His slaves and bestows peace and prosperity both in this world and in the Hereafter. Allah(swt) joins broken hearts and shows the true path to His slaves through Islam. This is the only religion in which all the rules and principles are crystal clear whether they pertain to faith, actions, character or behavior.\nIn brief, Islam:\nfamiliarizes all men with the names, attributes and actions of their Rab (Sustainer) and Creator.\nemphasizes that men should worship the One True God Allah(swt) and makes it clear that He(swt) has no partner. We should perform all the actions which He(swt) has ordered and abstain from all that He(swt) has forbidden.\nexplains about the life after death and what will happen on the Day of Judgement. That day will decide what the final destiny will be; that is whether one will go to heaven or to hell.\nThe main pillars of Islam are explained briefly in the following section.\nFirst:‘Iman’ meaning faith\nThis comprises six parts:\nBelief in Allah(swt):\nBelief in Allah(swt) means:\nAllah(swt) is the Rab(Sustainer) of each and every thing in this creation, He(swt) is the Creator of everything, He(swt) is our Lord, He(swt) is ruling over everything and He(swt) is the sole Sovereign of this entire creation.\nHe(swt) alone is worthy of worship. Other than Allah(swt), whatever is worshipped is pure myth.\nThe best and most beautiful names belong to Allah(swt). He(swt) possesses all the best attributes described in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith. While inviting people towards monotheism, Islam categorically condemns polytheism. And the people who worship anything or anybody other than Allah(swt) have been given the tidings of everlasting painful punishment in hell:\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ۖ وَقَالَ الْمَسِيحُ يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبَّكُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُ مَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَأْوَاهُ النَّارُ ۖ وَمَا لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنصَارٍ\nThey have certainly disbelieved who say, \"Allah is the Messiah, the son of Mary\" while the Messiah has said, \"O Children of Israel, worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord.\" Indeed, he who associates others with Allah - Allah has forbidden him Paradise, and his refuge is the Fire. And there are not for the wrongdoers any helpers.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-72)\nThat is the reason why Tawheed (monotheism) is the first pillar of Islam.\n‘Salah’ or ‘Namaaz’ is the second pillar of Islam. In fact salah constantly reminds us about ‘Tawheed’ and warns us not to let go of ‘Tawheed’ and stray towards ‘shirk’ because satan is after us trying to lead us astray right from the time when he along with Adam(as) were thrown out of heaven. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿قَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَإِنَّكَ رَجِيمٌ ٣٤ وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكَ اللَّعْنَةَ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ ٣٥ قَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنظِرْنِي إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ٣٦ قَالَ فَإِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنظَرِينَ ٣٧ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُومِ ٣٨ قَالَ رَبِّ بِمَا أَغْوَيْتَنِي لَأُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَأُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ٣٩ إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِينَ ٤٠﴾\n[Allah] said, \"Then get out of it, for indeed, you are expelled. And indeed, upon you is the curse until the Day of Recompense.\" He said, \"My Lord, then reprieve me until the Day they are resurrected.\" [Allah] said, \"So indeed, you are of those reprieved. Until the Day of the time well-known.\" [Iblees] said, \"My Lord, because You have put me in error, I will surely make [disobedience] attractive to them on earth, and I will mislead them all. Except, among them, Your chosen servants.\"\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verses-34-40)\nAfter bearing testimony about Tawheed, it becomes obligatory upon man that every form of worship like salah, charity, fasting etc. should be for Allah(swt) alone and no partner should be ascribed to Him be they angels, humans or any other form of creatures:\nإِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\nIt is You we worship and You we ask for help.\n(Quran, Surah-1, Al-Fatiha, Verse-4)\nقُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِينَ زَعَمْتُم مِّن دُونِهِ فَلَا يَمْلِكُونَ كَشْفَ الضُّرِّ عَنكُمْ وَلَا تَحْوِيلًا\nSay, \"Invoke those you have claimed [as gods] besides Him, for they do not possess the [ability for] removal of adversity from you or [for its] transfer [to someone else].\"\n(Quran, Surah-17, Al-Isra, Verse-56)\nBelief in angels:\nAngels are those creatures whom Allah(swt) has created solely for His worship. Angels are forever engaged in the worship of Allah(swt). They always obey Him. Allah(swt) has entrusted them with various jobs like:\nJibrail(as) has the job of carrying the revelations of Allah(swt) to the prophets. The job of causing rainfall is that of Michael(as). Israfeel(as) has the job of blowing the trumpet on Doomsday. One angel has the job of extracting the souls of men at the time of their death. Some people say that this angel is ‘Izrael’. But this is confirmed neither in the Holy Quran nor in Sahih Hadith. That is, all the angels are employed in doing what Allah(swt) has ordained for them. They have no power to do anything else.\nBelief in the books revealed by Allah(swt):\nFor the complete guidance of men, Allah(swt) has revealed various books from time to time to His prophets. The last book revealed by Allah(swt) is the Holy Quran which will serve as a guide to the entire human race till Doomsday. Some of the previously revealed books are mentioned in the Holy Quran. They are:\nTaurah which was revealed to Musa(as). This was a guidance for the Bani-Israel.\nInjeel which was revealed to Isa(as).\nZabur which was revealed to Dawood(as).\nSahifa or scrolls given to Ibraheem(as).\nBelief in the prophets of Allah(swt):\nAllah(swt) in His infinite mercy has sent many prophets for the guidance of humankind. The first of the prophets was Adam(as) and the last prophet was Muhammad(saws). All the prophets were created just like all men and have no attributes of the creator. They were the pious slaves of Allah(swt). Allah(swt) had bestowed a great favor upon them by making them His prophets. After Muhammad(saws), the chain of prophets has ended. No other prophet will arrive till Doomsday and so the religion propagated by him is for the whole mankind.\nBelief in the Day of Judgement:\nBelief in the Day of Judgement means believing that one day this world is going to come to an end. After that all the men will be resurrected and based on their deeds in this worldly life, they will be dealt with in a very just manner. Everlasting joy in paradise for the pious and obedient slaves of Allah(swt) and painful everlasting punishment for the disobedient wrong-doers.\nBelief in destiny:\nBelief in destiny means that Allah(swt) has created this world in His infinite wisdom. He(swt) is aware of each and everything that is happening in His creation. Everything is written out by Him and happens according to His wishes.\nSecond: Pillars of Islam\nIslam is based on five pillars without which no man is a complete Muslim. They are:\nKalima Shahadat: La-ilaha-illallah, Muhammadur-Rasoolullah which means bearing witness that none other than Allah(swt) is worthy of worship and Muhammad(saws) is His prophet. It means that since Allah(swt) is our Creator and Sustainer, He(swt) alone should and must be worshipped. Worshipping anything or anybody else is the greatest of sins. Muhammadur-Rasoolullah means that we should believe and follow the teachings of Muhammad(saws); that is, do what Allah(swt) has asked us to do through his prophet and abstain from what has been forbidden. The form of worship of Allah(swt) should be what Muhammad(saws) has shown us through his own example.\nSalah (namaaz): Allah(swt) has bestowed innumerable favors upon us. In return the least we can do is worship Him alone. It is Allah(swt)’s favor upon us that He(swt) has even explained the form of worship which will be liked by Him through the Holy Prophet(saws). Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّ الصَّلَاةَ كَانَتْ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ كِتَابًا مَّوْقُوتًا\nIndeed, prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-103)\nSo, offering salah five times everyday is obligatory upon us because Allah(swt) has ordered it. Salah is the best way of communication between Allah(swt) and His slaves. Because through salah, the slave calls out to Allah(swt), worships Him and supplicates to Him. If salah is offered in this way, it prevents men from all types of sinful activities. So, it is compulsory to offer the five salahs during one day plus one night(twenty-four hours). According to a Sahih Hadith, the one who does not offer salah becomes guilty of kufr (disobedience).\nAccording to another Sahih Hadith, the one difference between Islam and kufr is namaaz. For more information see ‘Salah’.\nZakat: This is a form of religious charity which must be given every year by every person for whom it is compulsory. It should be given to the needy people who have been described in the Holy Quran. In this way, the wealthy purify their wealth. They feel mercy and kindness for the poor and needy and a feeling of brotherhood is felt among all the people in the Muslim society. Neither will the wealthy loathe the poor nor will the poor envy the rich.\nAccording to a Sahih Hadith, “Zakat will be taken from the wealthy and distributed among the poor.” 2.5% of the value of gold and silver possessed and 10% of the agricultural produce if the source of water is rain or 5% if the water supplied is through artificial irrigation. For more information see ‘Zakat’.\nFasting: Fasting is the fourth pillar of Islam. The Arabic word for fasting is ‘saum’. It is obligatory for every Muslim man and woman to fast during the whole month of Ramadan. The fast begins just before sunrise and ends with the setting of the sun. During the day it is forbidden to eat or drink anything or engage in any sexual activity. Fasting cleanses both the body and soul and our sins get wiped out. It also escalates our position in the paradise. Fasting has many other benefits. For more information see ‘Fasting’.\nHajj: Hajj is the annual pilgrimage to Mecca. It is obligatory for every Muslim man and woman who has the financial means and physical ability, to perform Hajj at least once in his or her lifetime. It involves circumambulating the Holy Kaaba, travelling to Arafat where prayers and supplications are offered, staying in the tents in Mina, spending a night in Muzdalifah, stoning the pillars symbolizing the three satans etc. During the Hajj, everybody worships the Almighty Allah(swt) dressed alike and all differences of colour, wealth, status etc. cease to exist. For more information see hajj.\nThird: Teachings of Islam pertaining to the society\nIslam has laid down specific rules for the individual and social lives of men, which if followed will not only lead to a fulfilling worldly life but will also ensure success in the Hereafter. Marriage has been prescribed as halaal while adultery has been forbidden as haram. Similarly all good deeds have been encouraged while all the sinful ones have been forbidden. In spite of all the clear instructions, if man persists in doing wrong and perpetrating crimes against others, then a painful punishment awaits him. Adultery, intoxication, being unjust to the weak and orphans, murder, stealing, slander etc. will entail severe punishment. The severity of the punishment varies according to the severity of the crime. Islam has also made the relation between the ruler and the ruled very clear. The people should follow the orders of the ruler provided he does not go against the wishes of Allah(swt), because otherwise it leads to dissent and chaos.\nIn brief, we can state that Islam most beautifully makes clear the relation of the slave with his Master Allah(swt). It also explains the duties and responsibilities of an individual as far as his social life is concerned. There is no good which Islam does not encourage and no evil which it does not forbid. It is the best and most complete religion. But the people who do not have the complete knowledge about Islam try to defame it."],[164,"§Ismael(as)\n‘Ismael’ means ‘Allah(swt) has heard’. Ismael was the eldest son of Ibraheem(as). When Ibraheem(as) turned eighty-six and was still childless, he prayed to Allah(swt) and Allah(swt) heard his prayer and blessed him with a boy who was aptly named ‘Ismael’.It is believed that Ismael(as) was born in 2248 B.C. in a place near Habrun. About fourteen-fifteen years after Ismael, his second son Ishaq was born. Praising Allah(swt) for this gift Ibraheem(as) says:\nالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي وَهَبَ لِي عَلَى الْكِبَرِ إِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِسْحَاقَ ۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي لَسَمِيعُ الدُّعَاءِ\nPraise to Allah, who has granted to me in old age Ishmael and Isaac. Indeed, my Lord is the Hearer of supplication.\n(Quran, Surah-14, Ibraheem, Verse-39)\nAt another place, the description is as follows:\n﴿رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ١٠٠ فَبَشَّرْنَاهُ بِغُلَامٍ حَلِيمٍ ١٠١﴾\nMy Lord, grant me [a child] from among the righteous.\" So We gave him good tidings of a forbearing boy.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-100-101)\nThis forbearing child was Ismael. It is described in the Holy Quran that Ibraheem(as) had to face many trials and tribulations. Ibraheem(as) left Habroon along with his wife Hajira and son Ismael(as) and left them behind in the barren desert area of Mecca in Arabia. Hajira started following him and asked him as to why he was leaving them in that rocky place where there was absolutely nobody. But Ibraheem(as) did not even glance at her and continued on his way. Then Hajira asked him, “Has your Lord ordered you to do this?” Ibraheem(as) replied, “Yes.” Then Hajira replied, “In that case our Lord will not destroy us.”\nWhile returning from here Ibraheem(as) said:\nرَّبَّنَا إِنِّي أَسْكَنتُ مِن ذُرِّيَّتِي بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِي زَرْعٍ عِندَ بَيْتِكَ الْمُحَرَّمِ رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ فَاجْعَلْ أَفْئِدَةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِي إِلَيْهِمْ وَارْزُقْهُم مِّنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُونَ\nOur Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in an uncultivated valley near Your sacred House, our Lord, that they may establish prayer. So make hearts among the people incline toward them and provide for them from the fruits that they might be grateful.\n(Quran, Surah-14, Ibraheem, Verse-37)\nThen after some time the little water which Hajira had with her was exhausted and little Ismael started crying for water. Hajira got up and started searching for water. First she climbed the nearest mountain which was Mount Safa. But there was neither water nor any human being in sight. Then she came running down and climbed the adjacent mountain Marwa. In this way she made seven rounds between Mount Safa and Mount Marwa. (It is due to this reason that Muslims walk between Safa and Marwa during the Hajj and Umra). When she finally neared Marwa, she heard the voice of an angel. The angel dug a well using its feet and wings and water gushed out of it. This is the pure ‘zam zam’ water. From that day to this day, zam zam continues to flow out of that well. And the amount which flows out is more than enough for the lakhs of pilgrims who come there every day and even carry it back with them. The whole world is awed at this miracle spring right in the middle of a desert.\nIn this way Hajira and her son Ismael started living in Mecca. Then the tribe Jurham from Yemen came to Mecca. When they saw the spring over there, they sought Hajira’s permission to settle there and she agreed. When Ismael grew up, he married a girl from the tribe of Jurham. Then, Hajira passed away. She was buried in Mecca itself. Some scholars are of the opinion that both she and her son Ismael were buried near the Hijr, but there is no evidence of it. Once when Ibraheem(as) came to Mecca, Ismael(as) was out. So, he asked his wife, “How are you all?” She replied, “We are having a very difficult time.” He told her, ”When Ismael comes back, convey my salutations to him and also ask him to change the threshold of his house.” When his wife gave him the message, Ismael(as) understood that his father wanted him to divorce his wife. So, he divorced his wife and married another girl from the tribe of Jurham. Ibraheem(as) came back to Mecca again after a few days and asked Ismael’s wife, “How are you all?” She replied, “We are very comfortable. All praises be to Allah(swt).” He asked her, “What do you all eat?” She replied, “Meat.” He asked her, “What do you all drink?” She replied, “Water.” Ibraheem(as) prayed to Allah(swt) for meat and water. It is the result of that supplication that every person staying in Mecca definitely gets meat and water. Ibraheem(as) told her, “When Ismael(as) comes back convey my salutations to him and ask him to preserve the threshold of his house.” When his wife conveyed the message to him, Ismael(as) explained, “He was my father and he was referring to you as the threshold of the house. He has ordered me to keep you with me.” Then Ibraheem(as) and Ismael(as) together built the Holy Kaaba. (See Sahih Bukhari, Book of Prophets: 3364)\nFrom this we come to know that both the wives of Ismael(as) were from the tribe of Jurham. It is given in the Bible that Hajira brought Ismael’s wife from Egypt which appears to be untrue. Moreover, according to Tabri and other historians, the mother of the twelve sons of Ismael was the daughter of Syeda Mazaj-bin-Amr who was from the tribe of Jurham. The Arabs are from the tribes of Nabat and Khaider, the sons of Ismael(as). Prophet Muhammad(saws) was also from the descendants of Ismael(as). That is why the Jews called him ‘Ummi’, that is whoever was not from Bani-Israel was called ‘Ummi’. (See: Tariq Tabri, 2:314)\nAllah(swt) made Ismael a prophet. (See: Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verse-54)\nHe was sent as a prophet to the people of Amalique and Yemen. The Amalique tribe inhabited the region from Hijaz to Sina and Syria. This was one of the tribes of Arabia but its origin is not known. It is given in the Holy Bible:\nEsau’s son Eliphaz also had a concubine named Timna, who bore him Amalek. (Genesis, 36:12)\nIt is said that when Ismael(as) was one hundred and forty-seven years old, he passed away and was buried in Mecca near the grave of his mother Hajira. It is not confirmed by any Sahih Hadith that both Ismael and his mother were buried near the Kaaba at the Hijr. This is stated only by the historians like Tabri and Ibn-Kaseer etc."],[165,"§Isra\nThere are instances in the lives of the prophets when Allah(swt) favors them with the knowledge of certain hidden secrets of His creation. Examples of this mystic knowledge are ‘Isra’ and ‘Meraj’. The description of Isra occurs in the Holy Quran while that of Meraj occurs in many ‘Mu-ta-watir’ hadith which is referred to by more than thirty companions of the Holy Prophet(saws). ‘Isra’ means ‘to travel in the night’ which is mentioned in ‘Surah-tul-Isra’ also called ‘Surah Bani-Israel’. It says:\nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِي أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى الَّذِي بَارَكْنَا حَوْلَهُ لِنُرِيَهُ مِنْ آيَاتِنَا ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ\nExalted is He who took His Servant by night from al-Masjid al-Haram to al-Masjid al-Aqsa, whose surroundings We have blessed, to show him of Our signs. Indeed, He is the Hearing, the Seeing.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-1)\nAfter ‘Isra’ the Holy Prophet(saws) was given a tour of all the seven skies, during which he witnessed many miracles, a few of which are described in Surah An-Najm. Other than this, no other mention is made in the Holy Quran about this. But from the various books which were written about the life of the Holy Prophet(saws), we can deduce that this miraculous incident took place about one year before his migration from Mecca to Medina.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was returning dejected from Taif because the people there had rejected his message and had even stoned him due to which his feet were bleeding. The Holy Prophet(saws) was extremely sad and disheartened when the event ‘Isra’ took place through which Allah(swt) wanted to remove his despair and show him His miraculous signs so that the Holy Prophet(saws) would persevere in his gigantic task. Now let us have a look at what the Holy Prophet(saws) saw on this journey:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was relaxing near Masjid-e-Haram (Kaaba) when Jibrael(as) approached him. He woke him up and removed his heart which he then washed with the holy Zam-Zam water and then he brought it in a gold vessel filled with knowledge and put it back in its place. The incident of the washing of the heart of the Holy Prophet(saws) had also taken place when he was a child.\nThen he brought a mount which is called ‘Buraq’. It was white in color and bigger than a donkey but smaller than a mule. It was so swift that in one step it could cover the distance till the horizon.\nIn just a few moments they covered the distance from ‘Baitullah’ to ‘Baitul-Muqaddas’ which would normally take about forty days in those times. Then he led the prayer for the prophets.\nThen Jibrael(as) brought two cups – one containing milk and the other liquor. The Holy Prophet(saws) chose the cup of milk upon which Jibrael(as) said “You have chosen the natural thing. If you had chosen the cup of liquor, then your followers would have gone astray”. (Sahih Bukhari, 4709)\nThen Jibrael(as) took the Holy Prophet(saws) towards the sky. He(saws) met Adam(as) on the first sky, Isa(as) and Yahya(as) on the second, Yusuf(as) on the third, Idrees(as) on the fourth, Haroon(as) on the fifth, Musa(as) on the sixth and Ibraheem(as) on the seventh sky. Everybody welcomed him.\nOn this journey the Holy Prophet(saws) reached ‘Sidratul-Muntaha’ where no living creature can go. There he heard the sound of the pens of the angels busily writing the destiny of this world.\nFifty obligatory salahs in one day plus one night were ordained for him and his followers which were lessened to five upon the request of the Holy Prophet(saws). But the reward for these five salahs would be the same as that for fifty.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was asked if he had seen Allah(swt) during this journey to which he replied “He(swt) is a bright light. How can He(swt) be seen”. (Sahih Muslim, 178)\nOn this journey, the Holy Prophet(saws) saw Jibrael(as) in his real form and he had about 600 wings and covered the entire horizon.\nOn this journey, the Holy Prophet(saws) saw many great signs of Allah(swt). (See: Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-18).\nA few of those signs are:\nThere he saw a river on the bank of which was a mansion. Its bricks were diamonds and gems. When the Holy Prophet(saws) questioned Jibrail(as) about it, he replied “This is the river Kausar and the mansion which you see has been built for you by your Lord.”\nThere he saw ‘Baitul-Mamoor’ in which every day seventy thousand angels offered salah and on leaving the place they do not come again (it means that another seventy thousand angels arrive) (Sahih Bukhari, 3207)\nThere he saw four rivers, two of which were flowing through the heaven and two through this earth namely the Nile and the Euphrates.\nThere he also saw some people who were scratching their faces with their nails. The Holy Prophet(saws) asked Jibrail(as) as to who they were. Jibrail(as) replied, “These are the people who indulged in back-biting”.(Abu Dawood, 5:194)\nThere he saw both heaven and hell and their inhabitants and also the people who would go there in future.\nAllah(swt) demonstrated His greatness to His Holy Prophet(saws) with the help of ‘Isra’ and ‘Meraj’. He(swt) can do whatever He(swt) wishes. But this fact cannot be understood by the disbelievers. That is why when the Holy Prophet(saws) narrated these incidents to the people of Mecca, they made fun of him as described in Sahih Bukhari (Sahih Bukhari, 4710)\nThen Allah(swt) brought ‘Baitul-Muqaddas’ before the Holy Prophet(saws) and he started describing everything about it as though he could see it in front of his eyes.\nThis was the difficult period when in order to insult Abu-Bakr, the disbelievers of Mecca asked him “Have you heard about your friend who says that he has been to Baitul-Muqaddas and back in just one night?” Abu-Bakr replied, “If he says so what is so surprising about it? We believe that Allah(swt) sends revelations upon him. If he says he has been to and from Baitul-Muqaddas in one night, then we fully believe that it must have been true.” Hearing this the disbelievers of Mecca were surprised and the Holy Prophet(saws) bestowed the title ‘Siddique’ upon Abu-Bakr which means ‘truthful’.\nIf even today somebody does not believe in all these things, then he has not understood the great sovereignty of Allah(swt). First we should explain to him the truth about Muhammad(saws) being the prophet. When he accepts that fact then he will not disbelieve anything which the Holy Prophet(saws) says. As to the people who do not believe that Muhammad(saws) was a prophet, we request them to study Islam in depth.\nThere is a difference of opinion as to whether this journey was only that of his spirit or of both body and spirit. From the description in the Holy Quran, it is understood that it was of both his body and spirit. Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran :\nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِي أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى الَّذِي بَارَكْنَا حَوْلَهُ لِنُرِيَهُ مِنْ آيَاتِنَا ۚ إِنَّهُ هُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ\nExalted is He who took His Servant by night from al-Masjid al-Haram to al-Masjid al-Aqsa, whose surroundings We have blessed, to show him of Our signs. Indeed, He is the Hearing, the Seeing.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-1)\nIt is obvious from the description that some great event is being referred to. If the journey had been only of the spirit or maybe a dream, then there is nothing miraculous about it. Anybody can dream about it. And the disbelievers of Mecca had no reason to question it. Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nوَمَا جَعَلْنَا الرُّؤْيَا الَّتِي أَرَيْنَاكَ إِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلنَّاسِ\nAnd We did not make the sight which We showed you except as a trial for the people.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-60)\nThis proves that the Holy Prophet(saws) physically travelled to the heaven. If it was just a dream, it would not be a test for the people because we see the strangest dreams. In the Holy Quran the word used is ‘Rooya’ which also means a ‘dream’ but when the word ‘trial’ is used along with it, then the meaning would turn out to be ‘seeing it physically’.\nSome scholars have wrongly understood this journey to be a dream but when the initial verses of surah Bani-Israel are taken in conjunction with the sixtieth verse, it becomes clear that the journey took place physically. The Holy Prophet(saws) saw everything with his own eyes.\nWe believe all this to be true because Allah(swt) made the Holy Prophet(saws) perform this journey and Allah(swt) is the Greatest and Whose power encompasses the minutest part of this entire Creation. When He(swt) can create Adam(as) from dust, bring out Ibraheem(as) alive from the fire, split the sea into two for Musa(as), grant the power to perform many miracles to Isa(as), is it difficult for Him?\nIt is important to understand that we can fully comprehend the truth about ‘Isra’ and ‘Meraj’ only when we have absolute faith in the sovereignty of Allah(swt). Let us think about it. Today light is the fastest thing which has been discovered. Its speed is 186282 miles per second. Alpha Centauri is the star nearest to the Solar System and it takes 424 light years to travel to it and we haven’t yet crossed the first sky! Whereas during ‘Isra’ and ‘Meraj’, the Holy Prophet reached the seventh sky where ‘Baitul-Maamoor’ is present. No creature can go beyond that. Allah says in the Holy Quran:\nوَمَا أَمْرُنَا إِلَّا وَاحِدَةٌ كَلَمْحٍ بِالْبَصَرِ\nAnd Our command is but one, like a glance of the eye.\n(Quran, Surah-54, Al-Qamar, Verse-50)\nThat is, just as it takes hardly any time to blink our eyes, Allah(swt)’s order gets implemented immediately. Actually for anything to be done, Allah(swt) just says “Kun” (Be) and it is done. (Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-44)\nIn this way the Holy Prophet(saws) reached the first sky in the blinking of an eye and similarly he reached the second and the third skies and then he even reached the ‘Sidratul-Muntaha’. Here the speed of light was not enough and what came into effect was the command of Allah(swt) “Kun”. From this we understand that the journey ‘Isra’ was possible because of the command of Allah(swt) “Kun”. Before the Almighty’s command the theories of this world, time, astronomical distances etc. cease to exist. But only the truly wise can understand all this."],[166,"§Israel\nIsrael was the title of Hazrat Yaqub(as). This is a Hebrew word. In Hebrew, Israel is a person who fights the religious war along with Allah(swt). This has been explained in the Holy Bible also. (See: Bible-Genesis, 34:7). Another meaning of Israel is ‘Abdullah’. Israel is made of two words: ‘Isra’ meaning Allah(swt) and ‘Eel’ meaning slave. In the Bible, Bani-Israel have also been called Israel. (See Bible-Exodus, 32:4)\nIn Egypt some inscriptions have been found which date back to the time of the Pharaoh Minfatah, who ruled over Egypt from 1234 to 1227 B.C. In those also Bani-Israel have been referred to as Israel (See: Khamoos Kitab Muqaddas, p.69). From this, we can conclude that Israel was the title of Yaqub(as) and also that of Bani-Israel.\nReference has been made to Israel in the Holy Quran. The name Israel occurs only once in the Holy Quran:\nكُلُّ الطَّعَامِ كَانَ حِلًّا لِّبَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ إِلَّا مَا حَرَّمَ إِسْرَائِيلُ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِهِ مِن قَبْلِ أَن تُنَزَّلَ التَّوْرَاةُ ۗ قُلْ فَأْتُوا بِالتَّوْرَاةِ فَاتْلُوهَا إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ\nAll food was lawful to the Children of Israel except what Israel had made unlawful to himself before the Torah was revealed. Say, [O Muhammad], \"So bring the Torah and recite it, if you should be truthful.\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-93)\nThe reason for the revelation of this verse was that the Jews were opposing the Muslims saying that even though they claim to be following the religion of Ibraheem(as), they were eating the meat of camel which Ibraheem(as) and Yaqub(as) considered unlawful. The Holy Quran refutes this saying that everything allowed by Allah(swt) was lawful for the Bani-Israel, but that Yaqub(as) was forbidden from eating camel’s meat due to some illness.\nAccording to Tirmizi and Musnad Ahmad, Yaqub(as) abstained from the milk and meat of camel and later on the children of Israel followed suit considering it unlawful whereas the Taurah was yet to be revealed. As to what has been said in Leviticus and Deuteronomy:\nThe LORD said to Moses and Aaron, “Say to the Israelites: ‘Of all the animals that live on land, these are the ones you may eat: You may eat any animal that has a divided hoof and that chews the cud.\n“‘There are some that only chew the cud or only have a divided hoof, but you must not eat them. The camel, though it chews the cud, does not have a divided hoof; it is ceremonially unclean for you. The hyrax, though it chews the cud, does not have a divided hoof; it is unclean for you. The rabbit, though it chews the cud, does not have a divided hoof; it is unclean for you. And the pig, though it has a divided hoof, does not chew the cud; it is unclean for you. You must not eat their meat or touch their carcasses; they are unclean for you.\n(See Leviticus 11:1-8, Deuteronomy, 14:7-8)\nفَبِظُلْمٍ مِّنَ الَّذِينَ هَادُوا حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ طَيِّبَاتٍ أُحِلَّتْ لَهُمْ وَبِصَدِّهِمْ عَن سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ كَثِيرًا\nFor wrongdoing on the part of the Jews, We made unlawful for them [certain] good foods which had been lawful to them, and for their averting from the way of Allah many [people].\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-160)\nوَعَلَى الَّذِينَ هَادُوا حَرَّمْنَا كُلَّ ذِي ظُفُرٍ ۖ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ وَالْغَنَمِ حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ شُحُومَهُمَا إِلَّا مَا حَمَلَتْ ظُهُورُهُمَا أَوِ الْحَوَايَا أَوْ مَا اخْتَلَطَ بِعَظْمٍ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيْنَاهُم بِبَغْيِهِمْ ۖ وَإِنَّا لَصَادِقُونَ\nAnd to those who are Jews We prohibited every animal of uncloven hoof; and of the cattle and the sheep We prohibited to them their fat, except what adheres to their backs or the entrails or what is joined with bone. [By] that We repaid them for their injustice. And indeed, We are truthful.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-146)\nWe understand from above that all these things were lawful for the Bani-Israel just as they were lawful for the Muslims. It was also the religion of Ibraheem(as) and Yaqub(as); but the Holy Quran praises prophet Muhammad(saws) and says that when he (the Holy Prophet) arrives, the good and pure things which they had made unlawful will be made lawful again and they shall be relieved of the load which they themselves had placed upon themselves. (Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-157)\nAnd it has happened that more than one third of the world population has been freed of the shackles which bind them and as more and more people embrace Islam, more and more people shall be freed."],[167,"§Jaheem\n‘Jaheem’ means a blazing fire. The people who have rejected Allah(swt) and His commands will be thrown into this blazing fire. In the Holy Quran, a huge tree has been described whose roots are in the blazing fire:\n﴿أَذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا أَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّومِ ٦٢ إِنَّا جَعَلْنَاهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظَّالِمِينَ ٦٣ إِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِي أَصْلِ الْجَحِيمِ ٦٤﴾\nIs Paradise a better accommodation or the tree of zaqqum? Indeed, We have made it a torment for the wrongdoers. Indeed, it is a tree issuing from the bottom of the Hellfire.\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-62-64)"],[168,"§Jannat\n‘Jannat’ is a special word of the Holy Quran. This is called ‘Swarg’ in Hindi and Sanskrit and ‘heaven’ or ‘paradise’ in English. But the word ‘jannat’ on translation loses its comprehensive meaning. The description of paradise occurs in the religious books, but the way it has been described in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith is incomparable.\nSo, the description of paradise in the light of the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith is being presented here. Our original destination is paradise itself because that is where our forefather Adam(as) and his wife were expelled from.\nوَقُلْنَا يَا آدَمُ اسْكُنْ أَنتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ وَكُلَا مِنْهَا رَغَدًا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمَا وَلَا تَقْرَبَا هَٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونَا مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ\nAnd We said, \"O Adam, dwell, you and your wife, in Paradise and eat therefrom in [ease and] abundance from wherever you will. But do not approach this tree, lest you be among the wrongdoers.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-35)\nBut the Satan led them astray and caused them to be expelled from paradise.\nWe come to know from this story of Adam(as) that our original destination is paradise. As we cannot go to paradise in this worldly life, we can enter it after our death. This worldly life has been designed in such a way that all good deeds cannot be rewarded here; nor can all bad deeds be punished here. So, there has to be another life after this life where the pious and good people are rewarded with a life in heaven and all the wrong-doers are punished by a life in hell. If not, then in this world created by the Almighty(swt), there will be gross injustice. So, the existence of heaven and hell is a natural consequence of nature.\nThe Holy Quran is the last book of Allah(swt) in which the heaven and hell have been described in detail. Here the paradise has been described briefly.\nThe names of jannat:\nJannat has been described using various names in the Holy Quran. Each name has a special meaning. For example:\n‘Jannatun-Nayeem’ which means jannat which is filled with all sorts of wonderful things. ‘Jannatul-Quld’ which means jannat which is a permanent abode and the person who enters it stays there forever. Similarly ‘Jannat-e-Adan’ means ‘that which stays forever’. ‘Darrussalam’ is another name which means that the dwellers are forever in a state of peace and tranquility etc.\nLevels of jannat:\nThere are approximately a hundred levels of jannat. The highest level is ‘Jannatul-Firdous’. It says in one saheeh hadith that when you ask Allah(swt) for paradise, ask for ‘Jannatul-Firdous’ because that is the highest level above which is the throne of Allah(swt). (Sahih Bukhari, 2790)\nThe description of the people who shall go to Jannatul-Firdous:\nFor going to heaven the prerequisites are belief in Allah(swt), belief in His(swt) last Messenger(saws) and the path shown by him(saws) as mentioned in the Holy Quran.\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتُ الْفِرْدَوْسِ نُزُلًا\nIndeed, those who have believed and done righteous deeds - they will have the Gardens of Paradise as a lodging.\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-107)\nIt is possible that the word ‘Firdous’ and the word ‘paradise’ have the same origin.\nSix types of good deeds are described in the Holy Quran:\n﴿قَدْ أَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ ١ الَّذِينَ هُمْ فِي صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُونَ ٢ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُونَ ٣ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِلزَّكَاةِ فَاعِلُونَ ٤ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِفُرُوجِهِمْ حَافِظُونَ ٥ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ أَزْوَاجِهِمْ أَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُومِينَ ٦ فَمَنِ ابْتَغَىٰ وَرَاءَ ذَٰلِكَ فَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْعَادُونَ ٧ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِأَمَانَاتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُونَ ٨ وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ عَلَىٰ صَلَوَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُونَ ٩ أُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُونَ ١٠ الَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ الْفِرْدَوْسَ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ ١١﴾\nCertainly will the believers have succeeded: They who are during their prayer humbly submissive. And they who turn away from ill speech. And they who are observant of zakah. And they who guard their private parts. Except from their wives or those their right hands possess, for indeed, they will not be blamed - But whoever seeks beyond that, then those are the transgressors - And they who are to their trusts and their promises attentive. And they who carefully maintain their prayers - Those are the inheritors. Who will inherit al-Firdaus. They will abide therein eternally.\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Mu-minun, Verses-1-11)\nA few qualities of the dwellers of paradise:\nIt is compulsory to believe in Allah(swt), His(swt) Messenger(saws) and the path shown by him. After the advent of Islam, only those who whole-heartedly believe in Islam and completely enter its fold will enter paradise. The Holy Quran describes the deeds and qualities of such people at various places. A few are being described below:\nIn one surah of the Holy Quran, six deeds of the dwellers of paradise have been described:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ إِذَا فَعَلُوا فَاحِشَةً أَوْ ظَلَمُوا أَنفُسَهُمْ ذَكَرُوا اللَّهَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا لِذُنُوبِهِمْ وَمَن يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَلَمْ يُصِرُّوا عَلَىٰ مَا فَعَلُوا وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ ١٣٥ أُولَٰئِكَ جَزَاؤُهُم مَّغْفِرَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِمْ وَجَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا ۚ وَنِعْمَ أَجْرُ الْعَامِلِينَ ١٣٦﴾\nAnd those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves [by transgression], remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who can forgive sins except Allah? - and [who] do not persist in what they have done while they know. Those - their reward is forgiveness from their Lord and gardens beneath which rivers flow [in Paradise], wherein they will abide eternally; and excellent is the reward of the [righteous] workers.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verses-135-136)\nThe biggest attraction of jannat:\nThe biggest attraction of jannat is the sight of Allah(swt) which is impossible in this world. On the night of ‘Meraj’, the Holy Prophet(saws) went up till ‘Sidratul-Muntaha’ beyond which no living creature can go, but he(saws) could not have a glimpse of the Almighty(swt). Musa(as) also wished to see Allah(swt) and said:\nوَلَمَّا جَاءَ مُوسَىٰ لِمِيقَاتِنَا وَكَلَّمَهُ رَبُّهُ قَالَ رَبِّ أَرِنِي أَنظُرْ إِلَيْكَ ۚ قَالَ لَن تَرَانِي وَلَٰكِنِ انظُرْ إِلَى الْجَبَلِ فَإِنِ اسْتَقَرَّ مَكَانَهُ فَسَوْفَ تَرَانِي ۚ فَلَمَّا تَجَلَّىٰ رَبُّهُ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهُ دَكًّا وَخَرَّ مُوسَىٰ صَعِقًا ۚ فَلَمَّا أَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ تُبْتُ إِلَيْكَ وَأَنَا أَوَّلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nAnd when Moses arrived at Our appointed time and his Lord spoke to him, he said, \"My Lord, show me [Yourself] that I may look at You.\" [Allah] said, \"You will not see Me, but look at the mountain; if it should remain in place, then you will see Me.\" But when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He rendered it level, and Moses fell unconscious. And when he awoke, he said, \"Exalted are You! I have repented to You, and I am the first of the believers.\"\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-143)\nIt is obvious from above that it is impossible to see Allah(swt) in this worldly life. But among the bounties of paradise, the main attraction is the sight of Allah(swt) as explained in one sahih hadith:\n“You shall see Allah(swt) just as you see the moon. And there shall be nothing in between which may act as hindrance.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7434 and Sahih Muslim 633)\nAmong the bounties of paradise, one is that Allah(swt) will be forever happy with them. According to one sahih hadith, Allah(swt) will ask the dwellers of paradise if they are happy in paradise. The people of paradise will reply, “O Lord! Why will we not be happy when You have given us everything. Then Allah(swt) will say, “Shall I give you something even better?” They will ask, “What can be better than this?” Then Allah(swt) will reply, “Yes there is and that is my pleasure, I shall never be displeased with you.”\n(See Sahih Muslim, 2829)\nIt says in surah At-Tawba:\nوَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا وَمَسَاكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِي جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ ۚ وَرِضْوَانٌ مِّنَ اللَّهِ أَكْبَرُ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ\nAllah has promised the believing men and believing women gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide eternally, and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence; but approval from Allah is greater. It is that which is the great attainment.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-72)\nIt is the greatness of Islam that it regards both men and women on an equal basis. Both have a right to enter paradise. In the Holy Quran, Allah(swt) has given the example of the wife of Pharaoh (Firaun) to the believers:\nوَضَرَبَ اللَّهُ مَثَلًا لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا امْرَأَتَ فِرْعَوْنَ إِذْ قَالَتْ رَبِّ ابْنِ لِي عِندَكَ بَيْتًا فِي الْجَنَّةِ وَنَجِّنِي مِن فِرْعَوْنَ وَعَمَلِهِ وَنَجِّنِي مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ\nAnd Allah presents an example of those who believed: the wife of Pharaoh, when she said, \"My Lord, build for me near You a house in Paradise and save me from Pharaoh and his deeds and save me from the wrongdoing people.\"\n(Quran, Surah-66, At-Tahrim, Verse-11)\nThis is for the believing women that even they can enter paradise with the help of their good deeds.\nWe cannot imagine the bounties of paradise in this world as is explained in one sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) has created such wonderful things for his obedient slaves the like of which no eye has seen, no ear has heard and no mind has imagined. The fact is Allah(swt) has not acquainted anybody with those things.”\n(See Bukhari 3244, and Muslim 2823)\nThe same thing has been explained at one place in the Holy Quran:\nفَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَّا أُخْفِيَ لَهُم مِّن قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ جَزَاءً بِمَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ\nAnd no soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for eyes as reward for what they used to do.\n(Quran, Surah-32, As-Sajda, Verse-17)\nThe deeds which take us to paradise:\nTruth takes us towards goodness and piety and piety takes us towards paradise. When a person imbibes truthfulness, he shall be termed truthful. Falsehood takes us towards badness and badness takes us towards hell-fire. A person who lies shall be termed a liar.\n(See Bukhari 6094 and Muslim 2607)\nAccording to one sahih hadith:\n“You shall not enter paradise till you believe. And your belief is not complete till you love each other. Shall I tell you something by which you can love each other? It is: Spread salam among each other.” (Sahih Muslim, 54)\nAccording to one other sahih hadith: Abdullah-bin-Salam was a Jew of Madina. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to Madina, he also set out to meet him(saws). When the Jew saw the moon-like radiant face of the Holy Prophet(saws), he exclaimed that this cannot be the face of some false prophet. Abdullah-bin-Salam says that the first thing he heard the Holy Prophet(saws) say was:\n“O People! Spread peace, feed each other, pray at night when people are sleeping and you will enter paradise peacefully.”\n(Tirmizi 2485 and Ibn-Majah 1334)\n“Whoever is tested with girls and he treats them kindly, they will be a shield for him against the hellfire.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 1418 and Sahih Muslim 2629)\n“Let him be humbled into dust; he who sees either of his parents during their old age or sees both of them, but he does not enter Paradise.”\n(Sahih Muslim 2551)\nThat is, a person who hasn’t taken care of his parents whose reward is paradise.\nThe dwellers of jannat:\nThe majority of the dwellers of jannat will be those who were poor and weak in this world and the majority of the people of hell will be those who were proud and arrogant in this world. (Sahih Muslim, 2853)\n“The first group to enter paradise will be bright and radiant like the full moon. The second group will glitter like the stars. Every man in paradise will have two wives. No one will be unmarried in paradise.” (See Sahih Muslim, 2834)\n“The one who enters paradise will remain there forever. Neither will his youth pass nor will his garments wear out.” (Sahih Muslim, 2836)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“The dwellers of paradise will never fall ill. They will remain there forever. They will never die. They will remain young forever and never grow old.”\n(See Sahih Muslim 2837)\nA few attributes of jannat:\nThe jannat will be as wide as the earth and the skies:\nوَسَارِعُوا إِلَىٰ مَغْفِرَةٍ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا السَّمَاوَاتُ وَالْأَرْضُ أُعِدَّتْ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ\nAnd hasten to forgiveness from your Lord and a garden as wide as the heavens and earth, prepared for the righteous.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-133)\nIn one sahih hadith the Holy Prophet(saws) describes the extent of jannat as follows:\n“A tree in jannat will be so big that a person may walk in its shade for one hundred years without passing it.” (See Sahih Bukhari 4881 and Sahih Muslim 2826)\nIt is narrated in another Sahih Hadith:\n“Even if the person rides on a fast horse, he will not be able to reach the end of the shade.”\n(See Sahih Bukhari 6553, Sahih Muslim 2828)\nThe gates of jannat:\nThe gates of jannat have been described in three places in the Holy Quran:\nFirst: In surah Ar-Ra’d, the qualities of the true believers have been described like patient endurance, establishing prayers, combating evil with good etc. The reward for all these has been described as follows:\n﴿جَنَّاتُ عَدْنٍ يَدْخُلُونَهَا وَمَن صَلَحَ مِنْ آبَائِهِمْ وَأَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيَّاتِهِمْ ۖ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ يَدْخُلُونَ عَلَيْهِم مِّن كُلِّ بَابٍ ٢٣ سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُم بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ ۚ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ ٢٤﴾\nGardens of perpetual residence; they will enter them with whoever were righteous among their fathers, their spouses and their descendants. And the angels will enter upon them from every gate, [saying], \"Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. And excellent is the final home.\"\n(Quran, Surah-13, Ar-Ra’d, Verses-23-24)\nSecond: It has been mentioned in surah Sad that the doors of paradise will be opened for them:\n﴿هَٰذَا ذِكْرٌ ۚ وَإِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ لَحُسْنَ مَآبٍ ٤٩ جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ مُّفَتَّحَةً لَّهُمُ الْأَبْوَابُ ٥٠﴾\nThis is a reminder. And indeed, for the righteous is a good place of return. Gardens of perpetual residence, whose doors will be opened to them.\n(Quran, Surah-38, Sad, Verses-49,50)\nThird: In the surah Az-Zumar two groups have been described. The group which will enter hell and the group which will go to paradise. It is said about the second group:\nوَسِيقَ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ زُمَرًا ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءُوهَا وَفُتِحَتْ أَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَا سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ طِبْتُمْ فَادْخُلُوهَا خَالِدِينَ\nBut those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups until, when they reach it while its gates have been opened and its keepers say, \"Peace be upon you; you have become pure; so enter it to abide eternally therein,\" [they will enter].\n(Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-73)\nWe should pray to Allah(swt) that He(swt) in His infinite mercy grants us paradise."],[169,"§Jibrail\nJibrail is a word in the Suryani language which means a devotee of Allah(swt). This has been used for a specific angel who would bring revelations from Allah(swt).\nBoth in the Holy Quran and the Bible, Jibrail has been described at various places. For example in the Bible, while explaining the vision to the prophet Daniel and giving him the prophethood of seventy weeks. (See: Daniel, 9:21-27)\nSimilarly giving Zachariah(as) the good news about the birth of John. (See: Luke 1:11-21) and giving Maryam(as) the news about the birth of Isa(as) (See: Luke, 1:26-27)\nThis is the same angel Jibrail who first came to the Holy Prophet(saws) in the cave Hira with the revelation from Allah(swt). Jibrail would mostly appear in the guise of a human, but he appeared twice in his true form which is described as follows in the Holy Quran:\n﴿عَلَّمَهُ شَدِيدُ الْقُوَىٰ ٥ ذُو مِرَّةٍ فَاسْتَوَىٰ ٦ وَهُوَ بِالْأُفُقِ الْأَعْلَىٰ ٧ ثُمَّ دَنَا فَتَدَلَّىٰ ٨ فَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ أَوْ أَدْنَىٰ ٩ فَأَوْحَىٰ إِلَىٰ عَبْدِهِ مَا أَوْحَىٰ ١٠ مَا كَذَبَ الْفُؤَادُ مَا رَأَىٰ ١١ أَفَتُمَارُونَهُ عَلَىٰ مَا يَرَىٰ ١٢﴾\nTaught to him by one intense in strength - One of soundness. And he rose to [his] true form. While he was in the higher [part of the] horizon.Then he approached and descended. And was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer. And he revealed to His Servant what he revealed. The heart did not lie [about] what it saw. So will you dispute with him over what he saw?\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verses-5-12)\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) saw Jibrail for the first time in his real form in which he had six hundred wings, he appeared from the east and in no time spread over the entire horizon. The Holy Prophet(saws) saw him for the second time during ‘the journey of Meraj’. This is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ رَآهُ نَزْلَةً أُخْرَىٰ ١٣ عِندَ سِدْرَةِ الْمُنتَهَىٰ ١٤ عِندَهَا جَنَّةُ الْمَأْوَىٰ ١٥ إِذْ يَغْشَى السِّدْرَةَ مَا يَغْشَىٰ ١٦ مَا زَاغَ الْبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغَىٰ ١٧ لَقَدْ رَأَىٰ مِنْ آيَاتِ رَبِّهِ الْكُبْرَىٰ ١٨﴾\nAnd he certainly saw him in another descent .At the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary - Near it is the Garden of Refuge - When there covered the Lote Tree that which covered [it]. The sight [of the Prophet] did not swerve, nor did it transgress [its limit]. He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verses-13-18)\nIn the Sahih Bukhari, it has been narrated by Ibn-Masood that the Holy Prophet(saws) saw Jibrail in his original form and he had six hundred wings. (Sahih Bukhari, 4856 and Sahih Muslim 174/280).\nAisha(ra) said that the horizon was completely covered (Sahih Bukhari, 3735 and Sahih Muslim, 177/287)\nAisha(ra) has refuted the claims of the people who tried to prove from these verses that the Holy Prophet(saws) had seen Allah(swt) (Sahih Bukhari, 3234). Abu Zar himself asked the Holy Prophet(saws) if he had seen Allah(swt). The Holy Prophet(saws) replied:\n“He(swt) is a great light, how can He(swt) be seen.” (Sahih Muslim, 178/291)\nSo, it can be concluded that whenever Jibrail appeared he did so in human form except on the two above-mentioned occasions.\nOnce Jibrail said to the Holy Prophet(saws):\n“O Allah’s Apostle! This is Khadijah coming to you with a dish having meat soup (or some food or drink). When she reaches you, greet her on behalf of her Lord (i.e. Allah(swt)) and on my behalf, and give her the glad tidings of having a Qasab (palace in Paradise) wherein there will neither be any noise nor any fatigue (trouble).”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3820 and Sahih Muslim, 2432/71)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) once said to Ayesha(ra),\n“Look, this is Jibrail. He is greeting you.” Aisha(ra) said, “Convey my salam to him too.” Then she said, ”He could see and I could not see.” (Sahih Bukhari, 3217 and Sahih Muslim, 2447/91)\nHassaan-bin-Saabit was a famous poet. He recited poems praising the Holy Prophet(saws) and criticizing the tribe of Quraish. Once the Holy Prophet(saws) told him,\n“Recite more poems against them. Jibrail is with you.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3213 and Sahih Muslim, 2480/153)\nOne day the Holy Prophet(saws) was sitting with his wife Umme-Salma when a person approached him, spoke a few words and then left. The Holy Prophet(saws) asked his wife, “Do you know him?” She replied, “Yes, he is Dihyah Kalbi.” She later came to know that he was Jibrail who had come in the guise of Dihyah. (Sahih Bukhari 3633 and Sahih Muslim, 2431/100)\nWe come to know from various other hadith also that Jibrail would come in the guise of Dihyah, recite the revelations to the Holy Prophet(saws) and then go away. We also come to know from sahih hadith that one day Jibrail came to the Holy Prophet(saws) when he was seated in a congregation to teach him the basic principles of Islam. He questioned the Holy Prophet(saws) about various aspects of Islam like Imaan, Islam, Ehsaan and Doomsday etc. and then went away. After he left the Holy Prophet(saws) asked,\n“Do you all know who he was? He was Jibrail who had come to teach you the basic principles of religion.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 50 and Sahih Muslim,8)\nAnd we also come to know from the sahih hadith that Jibrail made the Holy Prophet(saws) offer salah on two occasions in order to teach him the correct method and timings of salah. In the year in which the Holy Prophet(saws) passed away, Jibrail recited the complete Holy Quran two times before the Holy Prophet(saws). (Sahih Bukhari, 6285 and Sahih Muslim, 2450)\nIn this way, Jibrail was a messenger from Allah(swt) to the Holy Prophet(saws) who revealed the verses from the Almighty(swt) to him. This does not mean that Jibrail was better than the Holy Prophet(saws). The Holy Prophet(saws) is the best among the creatures of Allah(swt)."],[170,"§Jihad\n‘Jihad’ means ‘to strive’. The word has been used in various contexts in the Holy Quran. A few of them are:\n1. Pressurise:\nوَوَصَّيْنَا الْإِنسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حُسْنًا ۖ وَإِن جَاهَدَاكَ لِتُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا\nAnd We have enjoined upon man goodness to parents. But if they endeavor (or pressurize) to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-8)\nIn the above verse, the word jihad is used to mean to put pressure on somebody.\n2. To strive hard:\nوَالَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا فِينَا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنَا ۚ وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَمَعَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ\nAnd those who strive for Us - We will surely guide them to Our ways. And indeed, Allah is with the doers of good.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-69)\nIn the above verse the word jihad is used to mean to strive hard. Similarly in the following verse:\nوَمَن جَاهَدَ فَإِنَّمَا يُجَاهِدُ لِنَفْسِهِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَغَنِيٌّ عَنِ الْعَالَمِينَ\nAnd whoever strives only strives for [the benefit of] himself. Indeed, Allah is free from need of the worlds.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-6)\n3. War:\nThe Holy Quran gives various reasons for waging wars. A few of them are:\n﴿أُذِنَ لِلَّذِينَ يُقَاتَلُونَ بِأَنَّهُمْ ظُلِمُوا ۚ وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ نَصْرِهِمْ لَقَدِيرٌ ٣٩ الَّذِينَ أُخْرِجُوا مِن دِيَارِهِم بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ إِلَّا أَن يَقُولُوا رَبُّنَا اللَّهُ﴾\nPermission [to fight] has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged. And indeed, Allah is competent to give them victory. [They are] those who have been evicted from their homes without right - only because they say, \"Our Lord is Allah.\"\n(See Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-39,40)\nIn the case of people who neither torment the Muslims nor fight with them, Allah(swt) does not forbid us from being good to them:\nلَّا يَنْهَاكُمُ اللَّهُ عَنِ الَّذِينَ لَمْ يُقَاتِلُوكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَلَمْ يُخْرِجُوكُم مِّن دِيَارِكُمْ أَن تَبَرُّوهُمْ وَتُقْسِطُوا إِلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِينَ\nAllah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them. Indeed, Allah loves those who act justly.\n(Quran, Surah-60, Al-Mumtahina, Verse-8)\nWhen the enemies fight with the Muslims:\nوَقَاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذِينَ يُقَاتِلُونَكُمْ وَلَا تَعْتَدُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ\nFight in the way of Allah those who fight you but do not transgress. Indeed. Allah does not like transgressors.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-190)\nWhen the disbelievers strive to change our faith and belief:\nوَدُّوا لَوْ تَكْفُرُونَ كَمَا كَفَرُوا فَتَكُونُونَ سَوَاءً ۖ فَلَا تَتَّخِذُوا مِنْهُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ حَتَّىٰ يُهَاجِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ فَإِن تَوَلَّوْا فَخُذُوهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ وَجَدتُّمُوهُمْ ۖ وَلَا تَتَّخِذُوا مِنْهُمْ وَلِيًّا وَلَا نَصِيرًا\nThey wish you would disbelieve as they disbelieved so you would be alike. So do not take from among them allies until they emigrate for the cause of Allah. But if they turn away, then seize them and kill them wherever you find them and take not from among them any ally or helper.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-89)\nHere we need to understand that the right for declaring a jihad rests with the ruler of the state who gives the call for jihad after analyzing the situation. This is not the prerogative of any one individual or group because jihad is one of the aspects of Islam, the implementation of which rests with the administration of the state. Just as the right for hanging a murderer or cutting off the hands of a thief or punishing a criminal etc. is that of the ruler, the right of calling for jihad also rests with him. And when the call for jihad has been given, it becomes obligatory for the citizens of that state to take part in it. As the Holy Quran says:\nانفِرُوا خِفَافًا وَثِقَالًا وَجَاهِدُوا بِأَمْوَالِكُمْ وَأَنفُسِكُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ\nGo forth, whether light or heavy, and strive with your wealth and your lives in the cause of Allah. That is better for you, if you only knew.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-41)\nThe people who try to escape taking part in the jihad have been criticized in the Holy Quran:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَا لَكُمْ إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمُ انفِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ اثَّاقَلْتُمْ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ ۚ أَرَضِيتُم بِالْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا مِنَ الْآخِرَةِ ۚ فَمَا مَتَاعُ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا فِي الْآخِرَةِ إِلَّا قَلِيلٌ\nO you who have believed, what is [the matter] with you that, when you are told to go forth in the cause of Allah, you adhere heavily to the earth? Are you satisfied with the life of this world rather than the Hereafter? But what is the enjoyment of worldly life compared to the Hereafter except a [very] little.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-38)\nAs mentioned before, jihad is a religious duty, the implementation of which is in the hands of the ruler. Without the consent of the ruler, it will not be jihad but a disturbance or riot and Islam is a peaceful religion, not a violent one. Therefore a few rules have been drawn up for jihad which the Holy Prophet(saws) taught the people who went forth for jihad:\nIn a war only those people can be killed who are fighting, namely the soldiers. The people who are not fighting in the war should not be killed.\nWomen, children, elderly people and priests should not be killed.\nA war should not be started during the night because that is the time when people are resting.\nBefore waging a war the enemies should be taught the principles of Islam so that if they understand and embrace Islam a war can be avoided.\nNo prisoner should be burnt in a fire.\nDuring a war no one should be bound and then killed.\nThere should be no plundering or pillaging.\nFields and orchards should not be destroyed.\nNo prisoner should be killed.\nA person running away should not be chased.\nIf a person shuts the door of his house, nothing should be said to him.\nAsylum should be given to the one seeking it.\nNo mailman or messenger should be killed.\nPrisoners should be treated well.\nPrisoners may be freed in exchange for Muslim prisoners.\nThese are a few rules of Islamic war. The Holy Prophet(saws) would educate the people going on jihad about these and asked them to implement the same.\nIt can be clearly seen that these are superior in all ways to the modern principles of war and if followed they can prove beneficial to the coming generations too.\nToday the powerful nations indiscriminately destroy the weak nations with the help of bombs and other tools of mass destruction killing thousands of innocents, annihilating cities and towns and maiming millions. What is worse is that the future generations also have to face the ill-effects of bombs and radiation for years to come."],[171,"§Jinn\nAllah(swt) has created two types of invisible creatures namely angels and the jinn. The creatures who represent nobility and goodness are called angels (For more information see ‘Angels’.)\nJinn are creatures some of which are good and some are bad.\nLet us study the origin of the word ‘jinn’. In Arabic ‘jinn’ means ‘to hide’. From this word are derived ‘junoon’ and ‘majnoon’ which means to hide one’s sense of reasoning. That is ‘majnoon’ is one whose good sense does not prevail and hence does whatever he pleases.\nOne other word which is derived from this is ‘janeen’ which means a child hidden in the womb of the mother. The word ‘jannat’ is also derived from this which means a dense garden which hides the earth.\nNo other religious book gives such a detailed description about jinn as the Holy Quran. Maybe this is because no other religion instructs the jinn while the Holy Prophet(saws) was sent as a messenger for both the humans as well as the jinn. So, it was important to know about these creatures in the all-encompassing religion Islam.\nWith the help of the Holy Quran, a few things about the jinn are being mentioned here. First let us discuss the things which differentiate the jinn from the humans:\nThe jinn have been created from fire while the humans have been created from mud. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ مِن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ ٢٦ وَالْجَانَّ خَلَقْنَاهُ مِن قَبْلُ مِن نَّارِ السَّمُومِ ٢٧﴾\nAnd We did certainly create man out of clay from an altered black mud. And the jinn We created before from scorching fire.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verses-26,27)\n﴿خَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِن صَلْصَالٍ كَالْفَخَّارِ ١٤ وَخَلَقَ الْجَانَّ مِن مَّارِجٍ مِّن نَّارٍ ١٥﴾\nHe created man from clay like [that of] pottery. And He created the jinn from a smokeless flame of fire.\n(Quran, Surah-55, Ar-Rahman, Verses-14,15)\nThis was the reason why Iblees refused to prostrate before Adam(as) and said:\nقَالَ لَمْ أَكُن لِّأَسْجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهُ مِن صَلْصَالٍ مِّنْ حَمَإٍ مَّسْنُونٍ\n\"Never would I prostrate to a human whom You created out of clay from an altered black mud.\"\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-33)\nWe also come to know from the above verse that the jinn existed on this earth before human beings. Then man was created who was a vicegerent of Allah(swt) on earth.\nThe jinn were given special powers not given to men. A jinn ‘Ifreet’ has been mentioned in the Holy Quran who says to Sulaiman(as) that he would bring the throne of the Queen of Sheba in no time:\nقَالَ عِفْرِيتٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَن تَقُومَ مِن مَّقَامِكَ ۖ وَإِنِّي عَلَيْهِ لَقَوِيٌّ أَمِينٌ\nA powerful one from among the jinn said, \"I will bring it to you before you rise from your place, and indeed, I am for this [task] strong and trustworthy.\"\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-39)\nSheba whose capital was Marib is situated about 55 miles north-east of Sana, the capital of Yemen. Sulaiman(as) was the king of Baitul-Muqaddas, Palestine which is at a distance of more than two thousand miles from Sheba. There was one other jinn with Sulaiman(as) who was more powerful than Ifreet. He said:\nقَالَ الَّذِي عِندَهُ عِلْمٌ مِّنَ الْكِتَابِ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَن يَرْتَدَّ إِلَيْكَ طَرْفُكَ ۚ فَلَمَّا رَآهُ مُسْتَقِرًّا عِندَهُ قَالَ هَٰذَا مِن فَضْلِ رَبِّي لِيَبْلُوَنِي أَأَشْكُرُ أَمْ أَكْفُرُ\nSaid one who had knowledge from the Scripture, \"I will bring it to you before your glance returns to you.\" And when [Solomon] saw it placed before him, he said, \"This is from the favor of my Lord to test me whether I will be grateful or ungrateful.”\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-40)\nHumans cannot move about in the skies without any support while the jinn can do so. They can even snatch a few words from there and convey it to men after distorting them. But they cannot reach the exalted assembly of the angels because as soon as they near it they are pelted with fire. (Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-8-10)\nBy the decree of Allah(swt) man can exist in only one form while the jinn can take on many forms and can even move from one place to another at great speeds. That is why the Holy Prophet(saws) has taught us the following supplication when we camp somewhere for the night:\n“A-oozu-bi-Kalimatillahit-tammatim-min-sharri ma Qalaq.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 2708)\n(I seek refuge in Allah(swt)’s perfect words from the evil of what\nHe(swt) has created.)\nOn reciting this, even if there are jinn at that place they cannot harm us in any way.\nAmong all men only Sulaiman(as) was given sovereignty over the jinn:\nوَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمَانَ جُنُودُهُ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ وَالطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ\nAnd gathered for Solomon were his soldiers of the jinn and men and birds, and they were [marching] in rows.\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-17)\nSulaiman(as) prayed to Allah(swt) and said:\nقَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَهَبْ لِي مُلْكًا لَّا يَنبَغِي لِأَحَدٍ مِّن بَعْدِي ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْوَهَّابُ\n\"My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me. Indeed, You are the Bestower.\"\n(Quran, Surah-38, Sad, Verse-35)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n\"Last night an 'Ifrit of the jinn suddenly appeared attempting to interrupt my prayer but Allah gave me power over him and I seized him. I wanted to tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque so that you could all see him in the morning, but I remembered the supplication of my brother Sulayman, 'My Lord, forgive me and give me a kingdom the like of which will never be granted to anyone after me.' So I sent him off in disgrace.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 461 and Sahih Muslim, 54)\nSulaiman(as) meant a kingdom in which there would be an army of jinn just like the army of humans and the jinn would work like the humans. The Holy Quran says:\nيَعْمَلُونَ لَهُ مَا يَشَاءُ مِن مَّحَارِيبَ وَتَمَاثِيلَ وَجِفَانٍ كَالْجَوَابِ وَقُدُورٍ رَّاسِيَاتٍ\nThey made for him what he willed of elevated chambers, statues, bowls like reservoirs, and stationary kettles.\n(Quran, Surah-34, Saba, Verse-13)\nThere is another school of thought which says that the jinn of a particular region follow the prophets who come to their region. That is the reason why they were familiar with the Taurah as mentioned in verse 30 of surah Al-Ahqaf.\nOne of the tasks of the jinn is that they whisper and cast doubts into the hearts of men as is mentioned in surah 114, An-Nas and we should recite this surah to seek refuge in Allah(swt) from these.\nNow let us discuss the common points between humans and jinn:\nAllah(swt) has created the humans and the jinn for His worship (that is to follow the path of ‘Tawheed’ or monotheism) (Quran, Surah-51, Adh-Dhariyat, Verse-56). The people who worship these jinn have been admonished:\n﴿وَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيعًا ثُمَّ يَقُولُ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ أَهَٰؤُلَاءِ إِيَّاكُمْ كَانُوا يَعْبُدُونَ ٤٠ قَالُوا سُبْحَانَكَ أَنتَ وَلِيُّنَا مِن دُونِهِم ۖ بَلْ كَانُوا يَعْبُدُونَ الْجِنَّ ۖ أَكْثَرُهُم بِهِم مُّؤْمِنُونَ ٤١﴾\nAnd [mention] the Day when He will gather them all and then say to the angels, \"Did these [people] used to worship you?\" They will say, \"Exalted are You! You, [O Allah], are our benefactor not them. Rather, they used to worship the jinn; most of them were believers in them.\"\n(Quran, Surah-34, Saba, Verses-40,41)\nIn fact, hell will be filled with both humans and jinn. (Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-119 and Surah-32, As-Sajda, Verse-13)\nJust as in the case of humans, there are both good and evil jinn. (Quran, Surah-72, Al-Jinn, Verse-11)\nAllah(swt) has given both men and jinn some powers and rights. Addressing both the creatures, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nيَا مَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ إِنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ أَن تَنفُذُوا مِنْ أَقْطَارِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ فَانفُذُوا ۚ لَا تَنفُذُونَ إِلَّا بِسُلْطَانٍ\nO company of jinn and mankind, if you are able to pass beyond the regions of the heavens and the earth, then pass. You will not pass except by authority [from Allah].\n(Quran, Surah-55, Ar-Rahman, Verse-33)\nJinn also stay with women just like humans:\nفِيهِنَّ قَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرْفِ لَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ إِنسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَانٌّ\nIn them are women limiting [their] glances, untouched before them by man or jinni.\n(Quran, Surah-55, Ar-Rahman, Verse-56)\nMessengers were sent to the jinn just as they were sent to the humans:\nيَا مَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ أَلَمْ يَأْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنكُمْ يَقُصُّونَ عَلَيْكُمْ آيَاتِي وَيُنذِرُونَكُمْ لِقَاءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هَٰذَا ۚ قَالُوا شَهِدْنَا عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِنَا ۖ وَغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا وَشَهِدُوا عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِهِمْ أَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا كَافِرِينَ\n\"O company of jinn and mankind, did there not come to you messengers from among you, relating to you My verses and warning you of the meeting of this Day of yours?\" They will say, \"We bear witness against ourselves\"; and the worldly life had deluded them, and they will bear witness against themselves that they were disbelievers.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-130)\nMuhammad(saws) was sent as a prophet for the whole world till Doomsday. So, just as the teachings of the other prophets who came before him stand annulled, the teachings of the prophets of the jinn also are no longer valid. So, the success of the jinn lies in accepting the prophethood of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nBoth the humans and the jinn have been challenged that even if they strive together they cannot produce a book like the Holy Quran. (See Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-88)\nLike the humans, the jinn also have no knowledge about the unseen contrary to what is popularly believed. This is negated in the Holy Quran as:\nفَلَمَّا قَضَيْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَوْتَ مَا دَلَّهُمْ عَلَىٰ مَوْتِهِ إِلَّا دَابَّةُ الْأَرْضِ تَأْكُلُ مِنسَأَتَهُ ۖ فَلَمَّا خَرَّ تَبَيَّنَتِ الْجِنُّ أَن لَّوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ الْغَيْبَ مَا لَبِثُوا فِي الْعَذَابِ الْمُهِينِ\nAnd when We decreed for Solomon death, nothing indicated to the jinn his death except a creature of the earth eating his staff. But when he fell, it became clear to the jinn that if they had known the unseen, they would not have remained in humiliating punishment.\n(Quran, Surah-34, Saba, Verse-14)\nThe jinn listening to the Holy Quran:\nIt is described in the Holy Quran about the jinn listening to the Holy Quran:\n﴿قُلْ أُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ أَنَّهُ اسْتَمَعَ نَفَرٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ فَقَالُوا إِنَّا سَمِعْنَا قُرْآنًا عَجَبًا ١ يَهْدِي إِلَى الرُّشْدِ فَآمَنَّا بِهِ ۖ وَلَن نُّشْرِكَ بِرَبِّنَا أَحَدًا ٢ وَأَنَّهُ تَعَالَىٰ جَدُّ رَبِّنَا مَا اتَّخَذَ صَاحِبَةً وَلَا وَلَدًا ٣ وَأَنَّهُ كَانَ يَقُولُ سَفِيهُنَا عَلَى اللَّهِ شَطَطًا ٤ وَأَنَّا ظَنَنَّا أَن لَّن تَقُولَ الْإِنسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلَى اللَّهِ كَذِبًا ٥ وَأَنَّهُ كَانَ رِجَالٌ مِّنَ الْإِنسِ يَعُوذُونَ بِرِجَالٍ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ فَزَادُوهُمْ رَهَقًا ٦ وَأَنَّهُمْ ظَنُّوا كَمَا ظَنَنتُمْ أَن لَّن يَبْعَثَ اللَّهُ أَحَدًا ٧ وَأَنَّا لَمَسْنَا السَّمَاءَ فَوَجَدْنَاهَا مُلِئَتْ حَرَسًا شَدِيدًا وَشُهُبًا ٨ وَأَنَّا كُنَّا نَقْعُدُ مِنْهَا مَقَاعِدَ لِلسَّمْعِ ۖ فَمَن يَسْتَمِعِ الْآنَ يَجِدْ لَهُ شِهَابًا رَّصَدًا ٩ وَأَنَّا لَا نَدْرِي أَشَرٌّ أُرِيدَ بِمَن فِي الْأَرْضِ أَمْ أَرَادَ بِهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ رَشَدًا ١٠ وَأَنَّا مِنَّا الصَّالِحُونَ وَمِنَّا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ ۖ كُنَّا طَرَائِقَ قِدَدًا ١١ وَأَنَّا ظَنَنَّا أَن لَّن نُّعْجِزَ اللَّهَ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَن نُّعْجِزَهُ هَرَبًا ١٢ وَأَنَّا لَمَّا سَمِعْنَا الْهُدَىٰ آمَنَّا بِهِ ۖ فَمَن يُؤْمِن بِرَبِّهِ فَلَا يَخَافُ بَخْسًا وَلَا رَهَقًا ١٣ وَأَنَّا مِنَّا الْمُسْلِمُونَ وَمِنَّا الْقَاسِطُونَ ۖ فَمَنْ أَسْلَمَ فَأُولَٰئِكَ تَحَرَّوْا رَشَدًا ١٤ وَأَمَّا الْقَاسِطُونَ فَكَانُوا لِجَهَنَّمَ حَطَبًا ١٥﴾\nSay, [O Muhammad], \"It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened and said, 'Indeed, we have heard an amazing Qur'an. It guides to the right course, and we have believed in it. And we will never associate with our Lord anyone. And [it teaches] that exalted is the nobleness of our Lord; He has not taken a wife or a son.And that our foolish one has been saying about Allah an excessive transgression. And we had thought that mankind and the jinn would never speak about Allah a lie. And there were men from mankind who sought refuge in men from the jinn, so they [only] increased them in burden. And they had thought, as you thought, that Allah would never send anyone [as a messenger]. And we have sought [to reach] the heaven but found it filled with powerful guards and burning flames. And we used to sit therein in positions for hearing, but whoever listens now will find a burning flame lying in wait for him. And we do not know [therefore] whether evil is intended for those on earth or whether their Lord intends for them a right course. And among us are the righteous, and among us are [others] not so; we were [of] divided ways. And we have become certain that we will never cause failure to Allah upon earth, nor can we escape Him by flight. And when we heard the guidance, we believed in it. And whoever believes in his Lord will not fear deprivation or burden. And among us are Muslims [in submission to Allah], and among us are the unjust. And whoever has become Muslim - those have sought out the right course. But as for the unjust, they will be, for Hell, firewood.'\n(Quran, Surah-72, Al-Jinn, Verses-1-15)\nIt is clear from the verses 8,9 and 10 that the incident of the jinn listening to the Holy Quran must have occurred in the initial days of prophethood of the Holy Prophet(saws) because when the verses started being revealed by Allah(swt), angels were appointed to prevent them being snatched by the jinn and the satans who would distort them. These verses refer to this. It is narrated by Abdullah-bin-Abbas in Sahih Bukhari (4921) and Sahih Muslim (882) that when the satans were prevented from obtaining information from the heavens, they sent out their people to find out why this was so. These people during their searches came to a place called ‘Naqla’ where the Holy Prophet(saws) was leading the Fajr (morning) prayer. When they heard the Quran being recited they exclaimed that this was the very thing which was the reason for their being stopped from hearing the information from the heavens. They went to their companions and told them that they had heard something wonderful. That is when surah-72, Al-Jinn was revealed.\nHafiz Ibn-Hazar in his famous book ‘Commentary on Bukhari Shareef’ has said that this incident took place in the initial days of the prophethood of Muhammad(saws). The second incident of the jinn listening to the Holy Quran is described in surah-46, Al-Ahqaf of the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ صَرَفْنَا إِلَيْكَ نَفَرًا مِّنَ الْجِنِّ يَسْتَمِعُونَ الْقُرْآنَ فَلَمَّا حَضَرُوهُ قَالُوا أَنصِتُوا ۖ فَلَمَّا قُضِيَ وَلَّوْا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِم مُّنذِرِينَ ٢٩ قَالُوا يَا قَوْمَنَا إِنَّا سَمِعْنَا كِتَابًا أُنزِلَ مِن بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ يَهْدِي إِلَى الْحَقِّ وَإِلَىٰ طَرِيقٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ ٣٠ يَا قَوْمَنَا أَجِيبُوا دَاعِيَ اللَّهِ وَآمِنُوا بِهِ يَغْفِرْ لَكُم مِّن ذُنُوبِكُمْ وَيُجِرْكُم مِّنْ عَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ ٣١ وَمَن لَّا يُجِبْ دَاعِيَ اللَّهِ فَلَيْسَ بِمُعْجِزٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَيْسَ لَهُ مِن دُونِهِ أَوْلِيَاءُ ۚ أُولَٰئِكَ فِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٣٢﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when We directed to you a few of the jinn, listening to the Qur'an. And when they attended it, they said, \"Listen quietly.\" And when it was concluded, they went back to their people as warners. They said, \"O our people, indeed we have heard a [recited] Book revealed after Moses confirming what was before it which guides to the truth and to a straight path.O our people, respond to the Messenger of Allah and believe in him; Allah will forgive for you your sins and protect you from a painful punishment. But he who does not respond to the Caller of Allah will not cause failure [to Him] upon earth, and he will not have besides Him any protectors. Those are in manifest error.\"\n(Quran, Surah-46, Al-Ahqaf, Verses-29-32)\nWe come to know from the above verses that the jinn already believed in Musa(as) and Isa(as). So, when they heard the Quran they exclaimed that this was the same thing which was revealed to Musa(as) and Isa(as).\nWe come to know from the hadith that this incident took place when the Holy Prophet(saws) was returning from Taif which was in the tenth year of his prophethood. The people of Taif had hurt him and caused him a lot of pain due to which he was very sad. This incident convinced him that not only humans but even the jinn were believing in him.\nAccording to Abdullah Ibn-Abbas the number of these was seven and they had come from ‘Nasibain’ in Turkey. (See Ibn-Kaseer 7: 272) and this incident also took place in Naqla because there is water there and is a fit place for setting up camp. Other than these two incidents there are many other instances when the jinn would come to the Holy Prophet(saws) to listen to his recitation of the Holy Quran. Sometimes the Holy Prophet(saws) would also go to them. We come to know from authentic narrations that seven such incidents took place.\nSpace constraint prevents a more detailed discussion on the topic. For more information see ‘Jaamiul-Kaamil’ by the author."],[172,"§Judi\nJudi is the name of the mountain on which the ark of Nuh(as) came to rest. European scientists have done a lot of research on this. They are of the opinion that these mountains are between Armenia and Iraq and that their name is ‘Ararat’ as mentioned in the Bible (Genesis 8:4) and one of its peaks is ‘Judi’ where the ark finally came to rest. (For more information see Nuh(as))."],[173,"§Jumua\nFriday is called ‘Jumua’ in Arabic. Before the advent of Islam this was called ‘Aruba’. Jumua is an Islamic name which is the sixth day of the week. The first day is Sunday. On this day Allah(swt) started the creation of this world and completed it in six days on Friday and then mounted His throne. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللَّهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ\nIndeed, your Lord is Allah, who created the heavens and earth in six days and then established Himself above the Throne.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-54)\nWe come to know from the sahih hadith that Allah(swt) created Adam(as) also on Friday. On the same day He(swt) admitted him into paradise. And it was on Friday that Adam(as) was expelled from the paradise. The Doomsday will occur on a Friday and on every Friday there is a particular time when Allah(swt) answers the prayers of His slaves.\nThat is, the day Friday has many special qualities. Before the advent of Islam the followers of Ibraheem(as) also believed in the importance of Friday and that includes Musa(as). Then when the Jews gave Allah(swt) a human form whom they called ‘Yehova’, they took Saturday to be sacred instead of Friday. Their reason was that because Allah(swt) rested on the seventh day after creating this universe in six days, even they would rest on the seventh day. And then they included the sayings of their prophets and other people in the Bible. Then Allah(swt) made Saturday sacred for them and decreed a severe punishment for them if they worked on that day. Referring to this the Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّمَا جُعِلَ السَّبْتُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ ۚ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ فِيمَا كَانُوا فِيهِ يَخْتَلِفُونَ\nThe sabbath was only appointed for those who differed over it. And indeed, your Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning that over which they used to differ.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-124)\nThat is, it would be made clear to them that actually according to the scriptures of Ibraheem(as), Friday was the important day, but they changed it to Saturday and then they violated the rule which they themselves had formulated and due to this they will face a terrible punishment. This is corroborated in a Sahih Bukhari hadith:\n\"We (Muslims) are the last (to come) but (will be) the foremost on the Day of Resurrection though the former nations were given the Holy Scriptures before us. And this was their day (Friday) the celebration of which was made compulsory for them but they differed about it. So Allah gave us the guidance for it (Friday) and all the other people are behind us in this respect: the Jews' (holy day is) tomorrow (i.e. Saturday) and the Christians' (is) the day after tomorrow (i.e. Sunday).\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 876 and Sahih Muslim, 855)\nThe Jews made Saturday sacred for themselves. They do no work on that day. Their religious scholars just study the religious scriptures. When Isa(as) saw the condition of the Jews, he criticized them severely and said:\n“The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath. So the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.”\n(Bible, Mark 2:27)\nOnce the Jews were angry with Isa(as) because he cured a man with a shriveled hand on a Saturday. (See Bible, Mark, 3:3-6)\nIn the initial days of Christianity some Christians considered Saturday sacred and then later on they made Sunday sacred because according to them the Messiah(as) came out of his grave on a Sunday. In 364 A.D. in the Christian conference, Sunday was declared sacred instead of Saturday once and for all. In this way both the Jews and Christians could not avail the special day which is called ‘Jumua’. The Messenger of Allah(swt) Muhammad(saws) directed us to this special day ‘Jumua’.\n‘Juma’ means to assemble. This day is so important that Allah(swt) revealed a surah named ‘Surah Juma’a’. The ninth verse of this surah says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا نُودِيَ لِلصَّلَاةِ مِن يَوْمِ الْجُمُعَةِ فَاسْعَوْا إِلَىٰ ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَذَرُوا الْبَيْعَ ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ\nO you who have believed, when [the adhan] is called for the prayer on the day of Jumu'ah [Friday], then proceed to the remembrance of Allah and leave trade. That is better for you, if you only knew.\n(Quran, Surah-62, Al-Jumu’a, Verse-9)\nHere by ‘remembrance of Allah’ is meant the Friday salah which has been made compulsory for each and every Muslim. In the sahih hadith the importance of this salah is greatly stressed. It is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“People must cease to neglect the Friday prayer or Allah(swt) will seal their hearts and they will be among the negligent.”\n(Sahih Muslim 865)\n“A Muslim who misses three Friday prayers due to laziness, Allah(swt) will seal their hearts.”\n(See: Ibn-Maaja 1126, Ibn-Khuzaima 1856 and Musnad Ahmad 14559)\nThe Friday prayer is not compulsory for a traveller, women, small children and the sick.\nA few things to be observed on a Friday:\n1. Every Muslim has to have a bath on Friday.\n2. It is sunnah to apply perfume on a Friday.\n3. We should try to reach the mosque as soon as possible.\n4. While entering the mosque we should bear it in mind that we do not hurt or inconvenience anybody. That is why we should not step over or push somebody but sit down wherever we find some place.\n5. If somebody goes out of the mosque for some reason then his place should be reserved for him because he has more right to it.\n6. If there is some space between two people and a third person wants to occupy it then those people should move a little so that enough space is made for him.\n7. Before sitting down it is sunnah to offer two rakat salah which is called ‘Tahiyatul Masjid’ which means ‘greetings to the masjid’.\n8. When the imam gives the khutbah (sermon) it is compulsory to listen to it carefully. It is forbidden to speak to others or engage in some other task during the sermon.\n9. On Fridays we must send the durood on the Holy Prophet(saws) as much as possible.\n10. The imam should not make his sermon very long but try to make it as brief as possible.\n11. When the imam stands up for giving the sermon and the call for prayer (azaan) is being given, it is forbidden to engage in any work. In the same way buying or selling are also forbidden.\n12. After the Friday prayer people can engage in their normal routine activities.\nJumu’a is actually the weekly festival of the Muslims. That is why on this day having a bath, wearing good clothes, eating good food, meeting and greeting each other, taking out the children for some amusement etc. are advised. But it is forbidden to do anything which goes against the teachings of Islam. For example watching movies, Muslim women adorning themselves and going out etc."],[174,"§Kaaba\nKaaba is also called ‘Baitullah’ which was built by Ibraheem(as) along with his son Ismael(as). It is the first house which was built solely for the worship of one Allah(swt) in Makka and it is the qibla towards which Muslims all over the world turn their faces while offering salah. It has one entrance which is called ‘Multazim’ and is at a height of about six-seven feet from the ground. Here the pilgrims offer supplications. At the south-east corner of the Kaaba is the ‘Hajr-e-Aswad’ which is a stone from paradise. Muslims kiss this stone. To the east of Kaaba is the ‘Maqaam-e-Ibraheem’ (the stone with the footprints of Ibraheem(as)) which is a great sign. Its description occurs in the Holy Quran. (Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-125 and Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-97).\nThere is an enclosure to the north of Kaaba which is called ‘Hateem’. It is in fact a part of Kaaba. Before the advent of Islam, when the Quraish were reconstructing the Holy Kaaba, they did not have enough lawful money to raise the Holy Kaaba on its original foundations and so they reduced it and left out the area of Hateem. We cannot offer ‘Farz’ namaz inside the Holy Kaaba and as Hateem is also a part of Kaaba, we cannot offer any obligatory prayer in the Hateem. This is the opinion of most of the scholars and moreover neither the Holy Prophet(saws), nor the Khaleefah-e-Raashideen nor the companions offered any farz namaz inside the Holy Kaaba. Sunnah salah can be offered inside. When the Holy Prophet(saws) triumphed over Makka and entered the Holy Kaaba, he offered two rakat salah. So, offering two rakat salah in the Hateem is the same as offering it inside the Holy Kaaba. When Aisha(ra), the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws) expressed her wish to pray inside the Holy Kaaba, the Holy Prophet(saws) led her by her hand to the Hateem and said,\n“If you wish to pray inside the Holy Kaaba, pray here because even this is a part of Kaaba but due to shortage of funds, the people of your tribe left it out of the Kaaba.”\n(Abu Dawood 2028, Tirmizi 876 and Nasai 2912)\nAccording to another hadith the Holy Prophet(saws) told Aisha(ra):\n“O Aisha! If the people of your tribe had not been new Muslims, I would have reconstructed the Kaaba and included the Hateem in it.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 1333)\nWe come to know from historical records that for about a thousand years after Ismael(as), Banu-Jurham were the custodians of the Holy Kaaba and after that the Quraish. Then a tribe within the Quraish became the custodians. During the victory over Makka, the key of the Holy Kaaba was with two people ‘Usman-bin-Talha-bin-Abi-Talha’ and his cousin (son of his paternal uncle) ‘Shaiba-bin-Usman-bin-Abi-Talha’. The Holy Prophet(saws) asked them to open the door of the Holy Kaaba, entered it, first cleansed it of the idols which it housed, offered two rakat namaz and then returned the key of the Holy Kaaba to them and said, “Till Doomsday, this should be with these people only. The one who snatches it will be a tyrant.” (Tabraani Kabeer, 11:20)\nThe sanad of this is weak but it is corroborated by other sanads. When in 42 A.H, Usman-bin-Abi-Talha passed away, the key came into the possession of Shaiba-bin-Usman-bin-Abi-Talha and till today it is with his family. They are the ones who open the Holy Kaaba and they are the ones who cover it with the ‘Ghilaf’.\nThis is the very same Kaaba, to destroy which the powerful chief Abraha had come from Yemen with a huge army which also consisted of many elephants. But Allah(swt) destroyed them on the way itself.\nThis incident is explained in Surah-Feel as follows:\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَابِ الْفِيلِ ١ أَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِي تَضْلِيلٍ ٢ وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ ٣ تَرْمِيهِم بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّن سِجِّيلٍ ٤ فَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَّأْكُولٍ﴾\nSeest thou not how thy Lord dealt with the Companions of the Elephant? Did He not make their treacherous plan go astray? And He sent against them Flights of Birds, Striking them with stones of baked clay. Then did He make them like an empty field of stalks and straw, (of which the corn) has been eaten up.\n(Quran, Surah-105, Al-Feel, Verses-1-5)\nThis is the same Kaaba due to which the tribe of Quraish were respected and were secure from hunger and fear. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَلْيَعْبُدُوا رَبَّ هَٰذَا الْبَيْتِ ٣ الَّذِي أَطْعَمَهُم مِّن جُوعٍ وَآمَنَهُم مِّنْ خَوْفٍ ٤﴾\nLet them adore the Lord of this House, Who provides them with food against hunger, and with security against fear (of danger).\n(Quran, Surah-106, Al-Quraish, Verses-3-4)"],[175,"§Kaaf-Haa-Yaa-Ain-Saad\nSee ‘Alif-Laam-Meem.’"],[176,"§Kaffara\nThe literal meaning of this is ‘hidden thing’. That is why the farmers are also called ‘Kuffar’ because they hide the seeds in the earth. As the Holy Quran says:\nكَمَثَلِ غَيْثٍ أَعْجَبَ الْكُفَّارَ نَبَاتُهُ ثُمَّ يَهِيجُ فَتَرَاهُ مُصْفَرًّا ثُمَّ يَكُونُ حُطَامًا\nHere is a similitude. How rain and the growth which it brings forth, delight (the hearts of) the tillers. Then it dries and withers away.\n(Quran, Surah-57, Al-Hadid, Verse-20)\nThe religious task undertaken as repentance for some sin committed is termed ‘Kaffara’. The Islamic meaning is the task undertaken as repentance for a sin and the consequent cleansing of the soul. In the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith, various sins have been prescribed various kaffaras. For example:\nKaffara for breaking an oath:\nThe oaths are of three types. The first type is the vain oath which some people out of habit keep taking without any intention of swearing. This is called ‘lagv’ in Arabic and this type of swearing is not binding in any way as Allah(swt) Himself says in the Holy Quran:\nلَّا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمَانِكُمْ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَاخِذُكُم بِمَا كَسَبَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ ۗ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ\nAllah will not call you to account for thoughtlessness in your oaths, but for the intention in your hearts; and He is Oft-forgiving, Most Forbearing.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-225)\nلَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمَانِكُمْ\nAllah will not call you to account for what is futile in your oaths.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-89)\nThe second type of oath is called ‘Ghamoos’ which a trader swears in order to sell his goods or to deceive some innocent person. This is a great sin and has been criticised in the sahih hadith.\nIt is narrated in Sahih Bukhari (6920) that a person once asked the Holy Prophet(saws) about major sins. He (saws) replied, “Ascribing partners to Allah(swt) (shirk) is the greatest sin”. He asked, “After that?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Disobeying the parents.” He asked, “After that?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Swearing a false oath.”\nThe punishment of the one who swears falsely is hell-fire. So, it is necessary that such a person asks forgiveness from Allah(swt) for his sins and decide not to commit them again.\nThe third type is the oath taken not to do good deeds. For example if someone takes an oath that he will not feed any poor people or help his relatives etc. It is imperative for such a person to immediately break his oath and not make it an excuse for not doing good deeds. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوا اللَّهَ عُرْضَةً لِّأَيْمَانِكُمْ أَن تَبَرُّوا وَتَتَّقُوا وَتُصْلِحُوا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ\nAnd make not Allah's (name) an excuse in your oaths against doing good, or acting rightly, or making peace between persons; for Allah is One Who heareth and knoweth all things.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-224)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“Pay the kaffara for breaking your oath and keep doing good deeds.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 6648, Muslim, 1649)\nThis is the kaffara of breaking an oath:\nلَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمَانِكُمْ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَاخِذُكُم بِمَا عَقَّدتُّمُ الْأَيْمَانَ ۖ فَكَفَّارَتُهُ إِطْعَامُ عَشَرَةِ مَسَاكِينَ مِنْ أَوْسَطِ مَا تُطْعِمُونَ أَهْلِيكُمْ أَوْ كِسْوَتُهُمْ أَوْ تَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ ۖ فَمَن لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ ثَلَاثَةِ أَيَّامٍ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ كَفَّارَةُ أَيْمَانِكُمْ إِذَا حَلَفْتُمْ ۚ وَاحْفَظُوا أَيْمَانَكُمْ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آيَاتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ\nAllah will not call you to account for what is futile in your oaths, but He will call you to account for your deliberate oaths: for expiation, feed ten indigent persons, on a scale of the average for the food of your families; or clothe them; or give a slave his freedom. If that is beyond your means, fast for three days. That is the expiation for the oaths ye have sworn. But keep to your oaths. Thus doth Allah make clear to you His signs, that ye may be grateful.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verse-89)\nKaffara for hunting in the state of Ehram:\nAnyone who goes to Makka in a state of Ehram with the intention of performing either the Hajj or Umra is forbidden from hunting. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَقْتُلُوا الصَّيْدَ وَأَنتُمْ حُرُمٌ ۚ وَمَن قَتَلَهُ مِنكُم مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَاءٌ مِّثْلُ مَا قَتَلَ مِنَ النَّعَمِ يَحْكُمُ بِهِ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِّنكُمْ هَدْيًا بَالِغَ الْكَعْبَةِ أَوْ كَفَّارَةٌ طَعَامُ مَسَاكِينَ أَوْ عَدْلُ ذَٰلِكَ صِيَامًا لِّيَذُوقَ وَبَالَ أَمْرِهِ ۗ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَمَّا سَلَفَ ۚ وَمَنْ عَادَ فَيَنتَقِمُ اللَّهُ مِنْهُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ ذُو انتِقَامٍ ٩٥ أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَحْرِ وَطَعَامُهُ مَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِلسَّيَّارَةِ ۖ وَحُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَرِّ مَا دُمْتُمْ حُرُمًا ۗ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ الَّذِي إِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ ٩٦﴾\nO ye who believe! Kill not game while in the sacred precincts or in pilgrim garb. If any of you doth so intentionally, the compensation is an offering, brought to the Ka'ba, of a domestic animal equivalent to the one he killed, as adjudged by two just men among you; or by way of atonement, the feeding of the indigent; or its equivalent in fasts: that he may taste of the penalty of his deed. Allah forgives what is past: for repetition Allah will exact from him the penalty. For Allah is Exalted, and Lord of Retribution. Lawful to you is the pursuit of water-game and its use for food,- for the benefit of yourselves and those who travel; but forbidden is the pursuit of land-game;- as long as ye are in the sacred precincts or in pilgrim garb. And fear Allah, to Whom ye shall be gathered back.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Maaida, Verses-95-96)\nKaffara for shaving the head in the state of Ehram:\nWhen in the state of ehram for hajj or umrah, kaffara has to be offered for shaving the hair of the head. If it becomes necessary either due to some disease or lice, then the kaffara is as described in the Holy Quran:\nفَمَن كَانَ مِنكُم مَّرِيضًا أَوْ بِهِ أَذًى مِّن رَّأْسِهِ فَفِدْيَةٌ مِّن صِيَامٍ أَوْ صَدَقَةٍ أَوْ نُسُكٍ ۚ\nAnd if any of you is ill, or has an ailment in his scalp, (Necessitating shaving), (He should) in compensation either fast, or feed the poor, or offer sacrifice.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-196)\nMore details about the compensation are not given in the Holy Quran. But we come to know them from the sahih hadith.\n“It is narrated by Kaab-bin-Ajra that when his hair was infested with lice and he was facing difficulties because of it, the Holy Prophet(saws) advised him to shave his head and as compensation to either fast for three days or feed six needy people or sacrifice whatever he can afford to (meaning camel, goat etc.)”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1815 and Sahih Muslim, 1201)\nKaffara for killing a Muslim:\nIt is a great sin to kill a fellow human being and an even greater sin to kill a Muslim brother. Such a person has been severely criticised in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith and a severe punishment prescribed for him. He will not only face the death sentence in this world but will burn in hell-fire in the Hereafter. (Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-93)\nBut if somebody has killed unintentionally, then the compensation is as described in the Holy Quran:\nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ أَن يَقْتُلَ مُؤْمِنًا إِلَّا خَطَأً ۚ وَمَن قَتَلَ مُؤْمِنًا خَطَأً فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ وَدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِ إِلَّا أَن يَصَّدَّقُوا ۚ فَإِن كَانَ مِن قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَّكُمْ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ۖ وَإِن كَانَ مِن قَوْمٍ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُم مِّيثَاقٌ فَدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِ وَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ۖ فَمَن لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ تَوْبَةً مِّنَ اللَّهِ ۗ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا\nNever should a believer kill a believer; but (If it so happens) by mistake, (Compensation is due): If one (so) kills a believer, it is ordained that he should free a believing slave, and pay compensation to the deceased's family, unless they remit it freely. If the deceased belonged to a people at war with you, and he was a believer, the freeing of a believing slave (Is enough). If he belonged to a people with whom ye have treaty of Mutual alliance, compensation should be paid to his family, and a believing slave be freed. For those who find this beyond their means, (is prescribed) a fast for two months running: by way of repentance to Allah: for Allah hath all knowledge and all wisdom.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-92)\nKaffara for Zihar:\nZihar means ‘the back’. In the pre-Islamic times, if an Arab said to his wife that she was like the back of his mother to him, then their marriage would be nullified and the wife would forever be haram to the husband. Once when a sahabi (companion) Ous-bin-Saamit pronounced ‘Zihar’ against his wife Khaula-bint-Maalik, she came to the Holy Prophet(saws) questioning him as to how they could separate at that age. Then, the 58th surah Al-Mujaadila was revealed in which it is explained that upon pronouncing ‘Zihar’ a wife does not become like his mother and mother is the one who has given birth to him and it is a sin to say so. And the wife remains haram till the kaffara is not offered. The compensation is:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ يُظَاهِرُونَ مِن نِّسَائِهِمْ ثُمَّ يَعُودُونَ لِمَا قَالُوا فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مِّن قَبْلِ أَن يَتَمَاسَّا ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ تُوعَظُونَ بِهِ ۚ وَاللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ ٣ فَمَن لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ مِن قَبْلِ أَن يَتَمَاسَّا ۖ فَمَن لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَإِطْعَامُ سِتِّينَ مِسْكِينًا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِتُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ۚ وَتِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ ۗ وَلِلْكَافِرِينَ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ٤﴾\nBut those who divorce their wives by Zihar, then wish to go back on the words they uttered,- (It is ordained that such a one) should free a slave before they touch each other: Thus are ye admonished to perform: and Allah is well-acquainted with (all) that ye do. And if any has not (the wherewithal), he should fast for two months consecutively before they touch each other. But if any is unable to do so, he should feed sixty indigent ones, this, that ye may show your faith in Allah and His Messenger. Those are limits (set by) Allah. For those who reject (Him), there is a grievous Penalty.\n(Quran, Surah-58, Al-Mujaadila, Verses-3-4)\nKaffara for having intercourse while fasting during the month of Ramadan:\nIt is obligatory to fast during the month of Ramadan. Fasting purifies the soul because by abstaining from food, drink, intercourse etc. from dawn till dusk just for the pleasure of Allah(swt), a Muslim proves that he is a true slave of the Almighty. Intercourse has been forbidden during fasting and if one commits this sin then firstly he should seek the forgiveness of Allah(swt) and in addition he should offer the compensation as narrated in the sahih hadith:\n“Once a person came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and told him, “I had intercourse with my wife while I was fasting. The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Free a slave.” To which he replied, “I do not own a slave.” Upon which the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Then fast for two months.” But the man said, “I do not have the strength for that.” Then the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Then feed sixty needy persons.” The man said, “I do not have so much money.” Just then another person presented the Holy Prophet(saws) with seven kilo dates. The Holy Prophet(saws) told the first person, “Take this and feed them to some poor people from your side.” The person said, “O Messenger of Allah! Between these two mountains there is no one poorer than me.” Upon this the Holy Prophet(saws) laughed and said, ‘Take them and distribute them among your family members.’\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1936 and Muslim, 1111)\nAnd this kaffara is obligatory upon the man only because it was due to his desire and not due to the desire of the wife.\nThe above incident throws light not only upon the compensation due when a person has intercourse while fasting, but also highlights the noble character of the Last Prophet(saws) because he was actually sent as ‘Rahmatul-lil-Alameen’ ( mercy to the whole world)."]])